Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: At sa mga kasamang ahensyang napapaloob dito,

asr-000706
01:05:20.548 --> 01:05:22.297
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: ang Armed Forces of the Philippines,

asr-000707
01:05:22.541 --> 01:05:23.598
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: ang Philippine Army,

asr-000708
01:05:24.066 --> 01:05:25.510
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: ang Philippine Air Force,

asr-000709
01:05:25.632 --> 01:05:27.584
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: at syempre ang Philippine Navy po.

asr-000710
01:05:28.601 --> 01:05:31.529
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Dadako na po ako sa aking magiging tanong.

asr-000711
01:05:32.241 --> 01:05:34.701
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: My question is about a report that

asr-000712
01:05:34.701 --> 01:05:38.402
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: China is recruiting Filipino government workers

asr-000713
01:05:38.402 --> 01:05:41.453
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: to leak official documents and information

asr-000714
01:05:41.453 --> 01:05:44.401
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: and turn them over to China.

asr-000715
01:05:44.401 --> 01:05:45.540
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: In a news report,

asr-000716
01:05:45.825 --> 01:05:48.611
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: between 2024 and 2025,

asr-000717
01:05:49.668 --> 01:05:52.332
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: may dating researcher ng Navy,

asr-000718
01:05:52.922 --> 01:05:55.138
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: may former employee ng DND,

asr-000719
01:05:55.443 --> 01:05:58.799
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: and a person close to the Philippine Coast Guard,

asr-000720
01:05:58.799 --> 01:06:01.747
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: ang nahuling nagsusulat ng analysis

asr-000721
01:06:01.747 --> 01:06:03.740
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: or nagpo-forward ng emails

asr-000722
01:06:03.740 --> 01:06:08.458
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: to handlers allegedly linked to the Chinese Communist Party

asr-000723
01:06:08.458 --> 01:06:10.573
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: in exchange for money.

asr-000724
01:06:11.244 --> 01:06:13.725
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Madam Chair, Mr. Secretary,

asr-000725
01:06:13.949 --> 01:06:15.718
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: paano tayo nalusutan po nito?

asr-000727
01:06:16.328 --> 01:06:18.056
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Can you detail to this committee

asr-000728
01:06:18.056 --> 01:06:20.110
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: how these Filipinos were recruited

asr-000729
01:06:20.110 --> 01:06:22.652
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: and anong klaseng mga impormasyon

asr-000730
01:06:22.652 --> 01:06:24.279
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: ang kanilang naibigay?

asr-000731
01:06:24.280 --> 01:06:26.221
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Doon po, sa alam ko,

asr-000732
01:06:26.544 --> 01:06:27.857
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: dito sa agency namin,

asr-000733
01:06:28.390 --> 01:06:31.225
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: sa internet lang po,

asr-000734
01:06:31.397 --> 01:06:33.490
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: nakatanggap ng mga email

asr-000735
01:06:33.490 --> 01:06:39.255
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: na kiniimbita sila na mag-sideline

asr-000736
01:06:39.255 --> 01:06:42.110
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: in various topics.

asr-000737
01:06:42.110 --> 01:06:43.347
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Kung pwede sila.

asr-000738
01:06:43.461 --> 01:06:47.324
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Kumuha ng paper sa sinasabing think tank.

asr-000739
01:06:48.313 --> 01:06:50.121
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: So dahil may pabuya ito,

asr-000740
01:06:51.262 --> 01:06:54.288
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: wala namang operational security protocols

asr-000741
01:06:54.288 --> 01:06:56.096
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: na mahigpit noong mga panahon na iyon,

asr-000742
01:06:57.142 --> 01:06:59.901
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: ito'y di o manay pinatulad

asr-000743
01:06:59.901 --> 01:07:06.219
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: hanggat sa nagkaroon ng mas detalyadong impormasyon

asr-000744
01:07:06.219 --> 01:07:10.767
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: ang hinihingi.

asr-000745
01:07:12.003 --> 01:07:15.638
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Naman ang Diyos po ay hindi na po pumayag

asr-000746
01:07:15.638 --> 01:07:20.376
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: sa pagkaalam ko itong mga bata at nagsuplong agad.

asr-000747
01:07:21.651 --> 01:07:24.277
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Pagamat ganon, marami pa pong mga

asr-000748
01:07:24.277 --> 01:07:28.768
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: sari-saring attempts as inventive as people are,

asr-000749
01:07:30.195 --> 01:07:32.098
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: the attempts to compromise are real.

asr-000750
01:07:32.954 --> 01:07:35.123
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: And at the end of the day po,

asr-000751
01:07:35.313 --> 01:07:38.206
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: nasa hygiene na po ng bawat empleyado

asr-000752
01:07:38.206 --> 01:07:39.766
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: at

asr-000753
01:07:39.766 --> 01:07:43.096
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: awa ng Diyos po, ito'y nasugpo

asr-000754
01:07:43.096 --> 01:07:48.386
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: at wala namang pong sensitibong impormasyon na napuha.

asr-000755
01:07:49.166 --> 01:07:51.925
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Ngunit ito po ay isa sa matinding paraan talaga

asr-000756
01:07:51.925 --> 01:07:52.953
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: kung papaano

asr-000757
01:07:52.953 --> 01:07:55.103
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: nang aakit

asr-000758
01:07:55.103 --> 01:07:56.892
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: ng researchers

asr-000759
01:07:56.892 --> 01:07:58.205
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: at ng mga

asr-000760
01:07:58.205 --> 01:08:01.059
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: particularly po

asr-000761
01:08:01.059 --> 01:08:03.209
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: kung hindi permanenteng employee

asr-000762
01:08:03.209 --> 01:08:05.588
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: kung job order or contract of service po

asr-000763
01:08:05.588 --> 01:08:07.909
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: dahil nga sa civil service regulation.

asr-000764
01:08:08.309 --> 01:08:14.398
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Ang baba po ng salary grades na mabibigay sa highly technical people,

asr-000765
01:08:15.121 --> 01:08:17.290
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: awa ng Diyos po,

asr-000766
01:08:17.709 --> 01:08:19.022
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: nasugpo po ito kaagad.

asr-000767
01:08:20.772 --> 01:08:21.477
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Ngunit,

asr-000768
01:08:22.066 --> 01:08:23.170
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: be that as it may,

asr-000769
01:08:23.836 --> 01:08:26.158
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: listo po palagi ang buong organisasyon

asr-000770
01:08:26.158 --> 01:08:28.213
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: sa mga kompromiso na maaaring ganito.

asr-000771
01:08:29.411 --> 01:08:31.695
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Di lang po naman sa atin nangyayari,

asr-000772
01:08:31.828 --> 01:08:35.158
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: marami pa pong mas delikadong impormasyon na napuha

asr-000773
01:08:35.158 --> 01:08:36.471
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: sa ibang mga bansa.

asr-000774
01:08:36.852 --> 01:08:48.878
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Lalo na based on capabilities na. At ito'y napro-prosecute ng mga countries involved at na pre-preempt.

asr-000775
01:08:48.878 --> 01:09:09.219
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: So, yung report po na yan, I cannot give further details, ngunit totoo po yan ang nangyayari po. Kami po ay magbabantay ng matindi sa ganito pong mga gawain. Thank you po sa tanong.

asr-000776
01:09:14.840 --> 01:09:22.900
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Maraming salamat po. Ito na lang po, paano na lang po natin masisiguro na ang DND, hindi na po ito mawawala?

asr-000777
01:09:34.799 --> 01:09:51.865
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Hindi po natin masisigurado talaga na hindi maulit. Pero ang importante, ang iaalam dun sa empleyado po, ang public platform, ang IT equipment na ginagamit, yan ay minomonitor.

asr-000778
01:09:51.865 --> 01:09:58.299
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: So, hindi pwedeng gamitin pang personal kung sino man empleyado, whether AFP or DND.

asr-000779
01:09:58.927 --> 01:10:12.840
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: At sinasubject din po natin sa matinding security vetting itong ating mga empleyado. Pero secondly po, ang hacking ay actually gera araw-araw po yan.

asr-000780
01:10:12.840 --> 01:10:22.508
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: So, there will be some compromises as with any organization dun sa IT system.

asr-000781
01:10:23.055 --> 01:10:30.116
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Ngunit, the exercise is to detect the compromise as soon as possible and to isolate it as soon as possible.

asr-000782
01:10:30.872 --> 01:10:40.105
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Kaya nga po, inulit po natin kanina na on the foundation pa lang ng isang sistema, kailangan pati hardware ay walang kompromiso.

asr-000783
01:10:40.105 --> 01:10:46.362
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Kung hindi, hindi nyo na mapapatch yan kahit kailan. Bubunutin nyo na po lahat yan. So, salamat po.

asr-000784
01:10:50.080 --> 01:11:02.319
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Can you also, Madam Chair, Mr. Secretary, can you also say to this committee na para hindi na-attract ang ating Filipino government workers sa mga alok ng China,

asr-000785
01:11:02.796 --> 01:11:11.219
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: we need to ensure our government workers are paid well, have secured benefits, and are able to exercise their rights and duties as citizens?

asr-000786
01:11:12.719 --> 01:11:18.086
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: No doubt about that, Madam Chair, Your Honor. No doubt about it.

asr-000787
01:11:18.753 --> 01:11:25.219
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: The civil service regulations and COA regulations allow us to adequately compensate people depending on skill level.

asr-000788
01:11:27.120 --> 01:11:36.980
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: And do you also support, Madam Chair, Mr. Secretary, the measures providing hazard pay for civilian government personnel deployed in the West Philippine Sea?

asr-000789
01:11:38.320 --> 01:11:42.312
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Sure. Yes, yes, Your Honor. Because they are subjected to risk also.

asr-000790
01:11:42.713 --> 01:11:47.699
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: And this includes civilian personnel too deployed in highly critical areas, for example,

asr-000791
01:11:48.730 --> 01:11:58.739
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: maybe teachers who are on duty in election areas, in identified hotspots, even first responders, Your Honor.

asr-000792
01:12:01.160 --> 01:12:12.802
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Masaya akong marinig ito mula sa ating Secretary dahil kami po sa Akbayan Reform Block ay nag-file po ng bill patungkol sa hazard pay po ng ating mga civilian personnel po.

asr-000793
01:12:13.255 --> 01:12:15.031
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Anyway po, Madam Chair, Mr. Secretary.

asr-000794
01:12:15.031 --> 01:12:16.925
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Kung may dadagdag ko lang po.

asr-000796
01:12:17.932 --> 01:12:19.767
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: I do not know how to approach the problem.

asr-000797
01:12:19.786 --> 01:12:31.487
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: And I do not know. The problem is, ang hazard pay po sa ating mga tauhan ay isang bagay yun.

asr-000798
01:12:32.612 --> 01:12:45.556
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Pero kung ang pinakamalaking inaalala din ng tao, paano may a-apply yung hazard pay pag yung pamilya ay may problema din?

asr-000799
01:12:45.556 --> 01:12:48.515
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Kasi psychological weight.

asr-000800
01:12:49.384 --> 01:12:49.897
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Po yun eh.

asr-000801
01:12:50.528 --> 01:12:55.560
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Let's say magre-respondi siya, alam niyang bahay yung bahay niya, mahirap din po eh.

asr-000802
01:12:56.053 --> 01:13:02.051
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: So, I really don't have the solution to the problem but it is something that we must tackle by the bull.

asr-000803
01:13:02.209 --> 01:13:03.669
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: The bull by the horns.

asr-000804
01:13:04.754 --> 01:13:16.850
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: So, maybe, you know, housing benefits for these people na alam niyang sigurado ang kanyang pamilya para sa ganon lubos-lubos yung pagbibigay ng serpisyo.

asr-000806
01:13:18.981 --> 01:13:20.954
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: So, yun lang po ang may dadagdag ko.

asr-000807
01:13:21.210 --> 01:13:23.361
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Sorry na lang po at wala po akong solusyon.

asr-000808
01:13:23.519 --> 01:13:25.374
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Pero I think it is a reality.

asr-000809
01:13:26.498 --> 01:13:29.734
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Nag-a-agree po ako sa inyo doon, Madam Chair, Mr. Secretary.

asr-000810
01:13:30.543 --> 01:13:36.719
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Nang sa gayon ay hindi na po sila yung tipong mabrive na lang ng kung sino mang bansa, no?

asr-000811
01:13:37.114 --> 01:13:42.481
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Na para lamang magbigay ng mga mahahalagang impormasyon.

asr-000812
01:13:42.481 --> 01:13:48.400
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: But anyway, Madam Chair, Mr. Secretary, do you have a credible information that some Filipinos,

asr-000813
01:13:48.578 --> 01:13:57.161
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: pin-elected officials, receive support from China and are releasing statements favorable to China's influence operations

asr-000814
01:13:57.161 --> 01:14:00.259
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: and expansionism in the West Philippine Sea?

asr-000815
01:14:03.280 --> 01:14:10.867
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: We have some ground to perhaps suspect it.

asr-000816
01:14:11.114 --> 01:14:20.685
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: But credible information in respect to evidence is kind of hard to adduce, particularly us, where

asr-000821
01:14:21.957 --> 01:14:23.932
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: We do not have access to bank deposits.

asr-000822
01:14:25.091 --> 01:14:31.852
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: I think it is best addressed by financial authorities, actually, Your Honor,

asr-000823
01:14:32.022 --> 01:14:41.879
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: in the same vein as a lot of syndicated activity was addressed in other countries

asr-000824
01:14:41.879 --> 01:14:46.854
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: through tax fraud investigations.

asr-000825
01:14:48.506 --> 01:14:50.102
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Our problem, really,

asr-000826
01:14:50.102 --> 01:14:52.532
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: is how much of this is admissible.

asr-000827
01:14:52.741 --> 01:14:55.134
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: At the end of the day, that's what counts.

asr-000828
01:14:55.723 --> 01:14:56.786
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: And we're not...

asr-000829
01:14:56.796 --> 01:15:02.436
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: And we're not prepared to make any statement on that score.

asr-000830
01:15:05.323 --> 01:15:12.900
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: We cooperate with law enforcement agencies on information, but that's the extent of what we do.

asr-000831
01:15:14.159 --> 01:15:15.021
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Thank you, Madam Chair.

asr-000832
01:15:15.021 --> 01:15:21.345
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: May maaari po ba kayong mabigay na informasyon dahil may mga speculations na po kayo na

asr-000833
01:15:21.345 --> 01:15:26.500
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: ano po kaya yung mga particular na nare-receive nilang mga support po?

asr-000834
01:15:28.400 --> 01:15:41.780
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: I'm also not prepared to state it, particularly if there are active law enforcement evidence-gathering operations at this stage.

asr-000835
01:15:44.239 --> 01:15:45.371
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Thank you, Your Honor.

asr-000836
01:15:45.616 --> 01:15:47.862
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: At huli na lamang po para dito.

asr-000837
01:15:48.447 --> 01:15:51.277
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Do you think that sa influence...

asr-000838
01:15:51.843 --> 01:16:00.580
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: sa operations po ng China sa social media, may mga elected officials din po ba na nag-a-amplify ng mga pro-China trolls?

asr-000839
01:16:02.239 --> 01:16:06.311
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: I think the statements speak for themselves.

asr-000840
01:16:07.354 --> 01:16:15.714
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: I believe, you know, there are some, undeniably, that the pronouncements speak for themselves.

asr-000841
01:16:16.206 --> 01:16:21.419
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: However, I'd like to point out too that the Chinese embassy website,

asr-000842
01:16:21.596 --> 01:16:26.868
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: itself, is not a diplomatic website anymore, but it is already a propaganda institution

asr-000843
01:16:26.868 --> 01:16:38.179
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: that enjoys the freedom of speech that we enjoy without extending reciprocal benefits to us in their own home country.

asr-000844
01:16:41.360 --> 01:16:43.405
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Tama po kayo, no, Mr. Secretary?

asr-000845
01:16:43.596 --> 01:16:48.299
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Hindi lamang po kayo yung nabiktima dyan dahil kami rin po nabiktima na rin dyan sa website na yan.

asr-000846
01:16:48.910 --> 01:16:52.638
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Anyway po, dadako naman po ko sa West Philippine Sea Security at saka yung...

asr-000847
01:16:52.772 --> 01:16:54.435
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: sa Maritime Security po.

asr-000848
01:16:54.435 --> 01:17:00.207
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Ang tensyon sa West Philippine Sea ay malinaw na security concern sa bansa.

asr-000849
01:17:00.762 --> 01:17:07.127
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Nito lamang July 20 of 2026, nasaktan ang dalawang Pilipinong sundalo sa Ayungin Shoal.

asr-000850
01:17:07.548 --> 01:17:18.003
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Sa harap ng ganitong sitwasyon, magkano ang aktual na pondong inilaan ng DND para sa pagpapatibay ng ating maritime security sa West Philippine Sea?

asr-000851
01:17:18.003 --> 01:17:20.871
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: At nakapaloob na po ba ito doon sa 64.3?

asr-000852
01:17:21.444 --> 01:17:26.739
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Rebuild yun na operations budget para sa Naval Force Defense?

asr-000853
01:17:30.320 --> 01:17:38.352
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Nakapaloob po yan sa regular operational budget ang ating kayang gawin sa West Philippine Sea.

asr-000854
01:17:39.546 --> 01:17:45.286
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: And hindi lang naman po doon, pati naman po sa northern portion, doon sa Bajo de Masinloc.

asr-000855
01:17:46.153 --> 01:17:47.212
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Hindi lang po naka...

asr-000856
01:17:48.214 --> 01:17:52.028
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Hindi lang po kami, kung hindi, Coast Guard at saka Philippine...

asr-000857
01:17:52.452 --> 01:17:57.517
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Navy ang nagtutulong dito.

asr-000858
01:17:58.057 --> 01:18:05.992
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: At importante din po, tulad ng alam po ng ibang mga kasamahan po na legislators,

asr-000859
01:18:06.551 --> 01:18:12.561
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: pag-asa-island, it's a question of habitation and normalization already of life in the area,

asr-000860
01:18:13.100 --> 01:18:16.625
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: which is an important part of that aspect.

asr-000861
01:18:17.646 --> 01:18:21.113
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: That's why we gave the instructions na rin po,

asr-000862
01:18:21.344 --> 01:18:24.734
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: sa ating WESCOM,

asr-000863
01:18:25.601 --> 01:18:37.620
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: na to fast-track the deployment of services by other agencies to pag-asa.

asr-000864
01:18:53.280 --> 01:18:58.183
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Kung ito po yung tingin ninyo at nakalagay na budget po ninyo sa NEP,

asr-000865
01:18:58.906 --> 01:19:02.399
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: sa tingin nyo po ba ito ay sapat para sa modernisasyon,

asr-000866
01:19:02.399 --> 01:19:07.199
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: dagdag deployment at protection ng sundalo at mangingisda sa West Philippine Sea.

asr-000867
01:19:07.200 --> 01:19:09.306
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Hindi po talaga ito sapat.

asr-000868
01:19:09.437 --> 01:19:12.878
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: At kung tutusin po natin, today, West Philippine Sea,

asr-000869
01:19:13.780 --> 01:19:18.536
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: mas malawak po ang ating Pacific Ocean boundary na kailangan din po natin bantayan,

asr-000870
01:19:19.175 --> 01:19:20.886
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: lalo na nandun yung Philippine Rise.

asr-000871
01:19:21.657 --> 01:19:27.466
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Tapos ang West Philippine Sea po ay kaalinsabay ngayon

asr-000872
01:19:27.466 --> 01:19:29.628
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: ng pag-file sa UN.

asr-000873
01:19:29.816 --> 01:19:37.693
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Nang ating delimitations across some features and Bajo de Masinloc.

asr-000874
01:19:38.483 --> 01:19:43.408
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: So, naging mas klaro ang mission area na kailangan tutukan ng pansin.

asr-000875
01:19:46.134 --> 01:19:51.662
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Kasama din po dito, in order to support West Philippine Sea operations,

asr-000876
01:19:51.662 --> 01:19:56.362
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: kailangan po natin ng base dito sa mainland.

asr-000877
01:19:58.016 --> 01:20:01.362
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Tatlong strategic passage po yan binabantayan.

asr-000878
01:20:01.550 --> 01:20:06.006
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Yung Verde Island Passage, of course, yung Batanes Channel,

asr-000879
01:20:06.532 --> 01:20:12.774
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Babuyan Channel, Verde Island Passage, at saka yung Surigao Strait Passage,

asr-000880
01:20:12.887 --> 01:20:15.913
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: at saka yung Sulusi na passage.

asr-000881
01:20:18.677 --> 01:20:25.689
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Yung po ang major transit points na actually nagdudugtong

asr-000882
01:20:25.689 --> 01:20:29.355
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: ng West Philippine Sea sa Pacific Ocean na tayo lamang ang meron.

asr-000883
01:20:30.859 --> 01:20:35.578
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: So, ito po ang dapat focus din ng ating operations

asr-000884
01:20:35.578 --> 01:20:40.560
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: na hindi natin magagawa ng lubos-lubusan kung wala tayong base.

asr-000885
01:20:40.561 --> 01:20:43.726
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Tama po kayo, Madam Chair, Mr. Secretary.

asr-000886
01:20:44.386 --> 01:20:48.606
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Ako po ay sumusuportan dito sa, lalong-lalo na kung ganito,

asr-000887
01:20:48.606 --> 01:20:52.374
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: na napapaloob na din yung sa operations budget ng neighbor.

asr-000888
01:20:52.411 --> 01:20:57.743
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: So, ito po ang global force defense yung ating plano para din doon sa West Philippine Sea.

asr-000889
01:20:57.950 --> 01:21:03.150
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: With that, Madam Chair, I'd like to manifest my support na dapat naman po talaga

asr-000890
01:21:03.150 --> 01:21:09.141
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: i-increase natin ang budget ng ating modernization or AFP modernization

asr-000891
01:21:09.141 --> 01:21:15.189
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: dahil hindi po ito makatarungan kung security po ng ating bansa ang pinag-uusapan.

asr-000892
01:21:15.189 --> 01:21:19.089
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: At huling katanungan na lamang po, Madam Chair,

asr-000893
01:21:19.089 --> 01:21:26.625
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: bukod sa halaga, paano niyo po natitiyak na mabilis at efektibo ang paggamit ng pondo?

asr-000894
01:21:26.625 --> 01:21:33.219
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Halimbawa, meron bang nakalaan na training, intelligence, at joint patrols po?

asr-000895
01:21:39.840 --> 01:21:47.309
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Bawat po acquisition natin, sinisigurado natin po, fully equipped na ang mga bagong gamit

asr-000896
01:21:47.309 --> 01:21:51.044
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: at sinasama na namin yung life cycle cost nito.

asr-000897
01:21:51.044 --> 01:21:53.845
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Sa costing ng bawat halaga.

asr-000898
01:21:53.845 --> 01:21:55.712
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Nang kinukuha.

asr-000899
01:21:55.712 --> 01:22:00.380
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: So dito po tayo malaki na nakakasigurado.

asr-000900
01:22:00.380 --> 01:22:04.115
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Tapos kumukuha na lang tayo sa original manufacturers.

asr-000901
01:22:04.115 --> 01:22:06.915
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Ayaw natin po ng middleman o consolidators.

asr-000902
01:22:06.915 --> 01:22:13.451
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Tapos meron pong long-term service contracts para nauuna po tayo sa supply chain palagi.

asr-000903
01:22:13.451 --> 01:22:20.920
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Hindi kada kung sino na lang ang magbibid for supplies na hindi man sila ang manufacturer.

asr-000904
01:22:20.920 --> 01:22:23.721
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: So yun po ang unang-unang guarantee natin.

asr-000905
01:22:23.721 --> 01:22:31.190
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Pangalawa, ang training po ay gasgas na rin po ang ating mga sundalo kaya hindi na rin po makapagbakasyon.

asr-000906
01:22:31.199 --> 01:22:38.229
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: At hindi lang po training ngayon, it's also knowledge.

asr-000907
01:22:38.239 --> 01:22:42.550
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Kasi hinihiwalay po natin yung knowledge sa skills.

asr-000908
01:22:42.560 --> 01:22:45.590
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Ang skills ay ang application ng knowledge.

asr-000909
01:22:45.600 --> 01:22:52.310
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Ang knowledge po yung bale, katawan ng knowledge.

asr-000912
01:22:52.320 --> 01:22:54.629
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Pinagkukuna natin ng skills.

asr-000913
01:22:54.639 --> 01:23:00.390
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: So nag-i-invest din po tayo sa knowledge, sa education ng ating mga tropa.

asr-000914
01:23:00.400 --> 01:23:08.149
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Lalong-lalo na po sa highly technical na mga subjects.

asr-000915
01:23:08.159 --> 01:23:20.310
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Kaya nga po tayo naglulungsad din ng direct commission program para makakuha tayo ng less physically fit but more highly technically qualified students.

asr-000922
01:23:26.400 --> 01:24:07.350
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Diyan po tayo kukuha ng skills training. Yun na po ang training na i-apply ng knowledge. At yan po matinding habilin na inilaan ng Departamento lalong-lalo na sa seleksyon ng magtuturo at sa liderato nito.

asr-000923
01:24:07.360 --> 01:24:09.669
Rep. Dadah Kiram Ismula: Thank you, Madam Chair.

asr-000923-split-1
01:24:09.679 --> 01:24:17.110
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Yes. Oh, yes. Congressman Pimentel, chairman of the Committee on Intelligence, is recognized.

asr-000924
01:24:17.120 --> 01:24:21.830
Rep. Alexander Ty Pimentel: I'll interject on a relevant point.

asr-000925
01:24:21.840 --> 01:24:23.830
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Yes, go ahead.

asr-000926
01:24:23.840 --> 01:24:39.259
Rep. Alexander Ty Pimentel: This is actually the reason, this is the event leading us to file the anti-spy unit law, a bill, an anti-foreign interference bill on all pending in the Committee of National Defense.

asr-000927
01:24:41.640 --> 01:24:48.724
Rep. Alexander Ty Pimentel: That's the problem mentioned by the Honorable Congresswoman.

asr-000928
01:24:49.128 --> 01:24:50.500
Rep. Alexander Ty Pimentel: Thank you, Madam Chair.

asr-000929
01:24:51.360 --> 01:24:52.872
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Yes, thank you, Congressman Pimentel.

asr-000930
01:24:53.439 --> 01:24:54.856
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Thank you, Congressman Ismula.

asr-000931
01:24:55.706 --> 01:24:59.060
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Next to interpolate, uh Deputy Majority Leader Arnan Panaligan.

asr-000932
01:25:01.867 --> 01:25:07.672
Rep. Arnan C. Panaligan: Thank you very much, Madam Chair. Good morning. Good morning, Secretary Teodoro and to our military officers.

asr-000933
01:25:08.110 --> 01:25:20.080
Rep. Arnan C. Panaligan: So, in the proposed 2027 NEP, the AFP modernization program was given 50 billion pesos without any unprogrammed appropriations.

asr-000935
01:25:20.080 --> 01:25:23.062
Rep. Arnan C. Panaligan: I'm sure this will affect your Horizon 3.

asr-000936
01:25:23.652 --> 01:25:26.133
Rep. Arnan C. Panaligan: And you mentioned that you will revise it again.

asr-000937
01:25:26.538 --> 01:25:30.554
Rep. Arnan C. Panaligan: So, this has undergone many re-horizoning, yung Horizon 3.

asr-000938
01:25:31.027 --> 01:25:46.231
Rep. Arnan C. Panaligan: Could you please inform us now, yung mga na-charge na dun sa 40 billion pesos for 2026, kung may natitira pa, and your proposal for 2027,

asr-000940
01:25:46.501 --> 01:25:55.462
Rep. Arnan C. Panaligan: What particular items are you going to charge for the 50 billion pesos proposed in 2027?

asr-000941
01:26:02.060 --> 01:26:09.350
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Hindi. Sa 50, your honor, lahat ay obligated dahil pambayad ng MAICA. So, walang bago yun.

asr-000942
01:26:11.037 --> 01:26:15.155
Rep. Arnan C. Panaligan: So, that's for the 50 billion for next year?

asr-000943
01:26:15.760 --> 01:26:16.080
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Yes.

asr-000944
01:26:16.080 --> 01:26:19.610
Rep. Arnan C. Panaligan: And how about for the 40 billion for this year, also for MAICA?

asr-000945
01:26:20.740 --> 01:26:21.601
Rep. Arnan C. Panaligan: Ano yung unprogrammed?

asr-000946
01:26:23.963 --> 01:26:26.550
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Wala pang unprogrammed.

asr-000947
01:26:26.560 --> 01:26:28.621
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Yes, your honor. Nasa 21.

asr-000948
01:26:29.650 --> 01:26:32.013
Rep. Arnan C. Panaligan: For 2026?

asr-000949
01:26:32.114 --> 01:26:33.346
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Yes, your honor.

asr-000950
01:26:34.308 --> 01:26:40.467
Rep. Arnan C. Panaligan: In the last hearing of the DBCC, first day of the budget hearing, I asked Secretary De Leon of DBM,

asr-000951
01:26:41.142 --> 01:26:47.285
Rep. Arnan C. Panaligan: if narilis na yung 50 billion unprogrammed funding for this year. So, sabi niya wala pa.

asr-000952
01:26:47.723 --> 01:26:52.079
Rep. Arnan C. Panaligan: And when I asked him kung may possibility na marilis, of course, sabi niya two conditions.

asr-000953
01:26:52.080 --> 01:26:55.672
Rep. Arnan C. Panaligan: First, excess revenues, and second, kung kailangan pa rin ng DND.

asr-000954
01:26:56.043 --> 01:26:57.562
Rep. Arnan C. Panaligan: So, I'm sure kailangan yun, ano?

asr-000955
01:26:58.051 --> 01:27:03.839
Rep. Arnan C. Panaligan: So, I hope that you can make a strong representation sa kanila para kung kailangan talaga ninyo,

asr-000956
01:27:04.261 --> 01:27:09.037
Rep. Arnan C. Panaligan: they can do something about it para ma-access ninyo yung unprogrammed funds of 50 billion for this year.

asr-000957
01:27:09.273 --> 01:27:11.973
Rep. Arnan C. Panaligan: Considering hindi sila nagbigay ng unprogrammed funds for next year.

asr-000958
01:27:11.973 --> 01:27:23.482
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Ang tala lang po dyan sa excess, yung damages po na nangyari po dito sa mga sunod-sunod na habagar at saka sa lindol dun sa Mindanao,

asr-000959
01:27:24.562 --> 01:27:26.350
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: yung po malaking.

asr-000960
01:27:27.228 --> 01:27:27.937
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Cost, no?

asr-000961
01:27:28.190 --> 01:27:37.893
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Inaasahan pa po natin na magkakaroon ng additional na weather disturbances until the end of the year.

asr-000962
01:27:38.315 --> 01:27:44.356
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Dun lang nga po sa Occidental Mindoro, may bumahan na nga po ng katakot-takot.

asr-000963
01:27:45.065 --> 01:27:48.068
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: So, dun po siguro kung meron man, maantala yung excess.

asr-000964
01:27:49.385 --> 01:27:55.439
Rep. Arnan C. Panaligan: Madam Chair, can I request that we be furnished with a copy of the items charged?

asr-000965
01:27:55.440 --> 01:28:00.404
Rep. Arnan C. Panaligan: 40 billion and sa proposal na 50 billion for next year, kahit yun ay for MAICA.

asr-000966
01:28:00.860 --> 01:28:07.119
Rep. Arnan C. Panaligan: Now, Madam Chair, Mr. Secretary, at the budget hearing last year, you mentioned that because of budget constraints,

asr-000967
01:28:07.119 --> 01:28:14.258
Rep. Arnan C. Panaligan: you preferred that the DND and AFP be allowed to obtain loans to finance your modernization projects, no?

asr-000968
01:28:14.866 --> 01:28:24.940
Rep. Arnan C. Panaligan: And you suggested the amendment of PD 415, a 1974 PD that set the ceiling for loans at 300 million US dollars.

asr-000969
01:28:25.177 --> 01:28:26.712
Rep. Arnan C. Panaligan: 1974 exchange rate.

asr-000970
01:28:27.252 --> 01:28:36.533
Rep. Arnan C. Panaligan: So, in response to your proposal, I filed House Bill No. 8059, increasing the ceiling to 1 billion US dollars for a single project.

asr-000971
01:28:36.905 --> 01:28:39.503
Rep. Arnan C. Panaligan: But it could be revised, no?

asr-000972
01:28:39.807 --> 01:28:41.512
Rep. Arnan C. Panaligan: And remove the ceiling altogether.

asr-000973
01:28:42.035 --> 01:28:45.258
Rep. Arnan C. Panaligan: Now, dun sa 27NEP kasi inalis din yung special provision.

asr-000974
01:28:45.798 --> 01:28:50.405
Rep. Arnan C. Panaligan: So, yung DBM, hindi na kayo binigyan ng malaki for modernization, inalis pa yung authority, no?

asr-000975
01:28:50.877 --> 01:28:52.548
Rep. Arnan C. Panaligan: Na kayo ay mag-loan.

asr-000976
01:28:52.733 --> 01:28:54.742
Rep. Arnan C. Panaligan: So, better talaga, merong law.

asr-000977
01:28:55.113 --> 01:28:56.716
Rep. Arnan C. Panaligan: That will authorize you.

asr-000978
01:28:57.020 --> 01:28:59.052
Rep. Arnan C. Panaligan: That's the rationale for my House Bill 8059.

asr-000979
01:28:59.062 --> 01:29:00.968
Rep. Arnan C. Panaligan: So, which do you prefer?

asr-000980
01:29:01.188 --> 01:29:06.807
Rep. Arnan C. Panaligan: Wala ng ceiling altogether or may cap pa rin, let's say, from 300 to a billion dollars or so?

asr-000981
01:29:07.195 --> 01:29:20.480
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Wala ng cap, your Honor, because the DBM and the DOF sets the cap, actually, based on the fiscal condition of the country

asr-000982
01:29:20.480 --> 01:29:25.110
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: and the type of loan which will be approved by them anyway.

asr-000983
01:29:25.120 --> 01:29:29.032
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: That will be entered into.

asr-000984
01:29:29.977 --> 01:29:41.620
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: So, actually, they have total control over the financial accommodation or financial arrangement that is going to be made.

asr-000985
01:29:42.633 --> 01:29:48.421
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: They will set the ceiling, anyway, depending on what the country can afford.

asr-000986
01:29:49.282 --> 01:29:55.190
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: And since the loan will be entered into by...

asr-000987
01:29:55.199 --> 01:29:56.318
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: The DOF.

asr-000988
01:29:56.400 --> 01:29:57.100
Rep. Arnan C. Panaligan: Thank you.

asr-000989
01:29:57.230 --> 01:30:10.880
Rep. Arnan C. Panaligan: The DOF, at the end of the day, I think that is a sufficient guarantee because for the fiscal ability of the government to service the debt,

asr-000990
01:30:10.880 --> 01:30:17.598
Rep. Arnan C. Panaligan: given the fact that revenue raising is the prime mandate of the DOF.

asr-000991
01:30:18.442 --> 01:30:24.533
Rep. Arnan C. Panaligan: Well, I was assured by the Chair of the Committee on National Defense that the Committee will deliberate soon on that House bill

asr-000992
01:30:24.770 --> 01:30:27.198
Rep. Arnan C. Panaligan: and he assigned me to head the Technical Working Group.

asr-000993
01:30:27.199 --> 01:30:29.984
Rep. Arnan C. Panaligan: So, we will discuss this further at the TWG.

asr-000994
01:30:30.625 --> 01:30:35.030
Rep. Arnan C. Panaligan: And I have here a copy of the U.S. Senate bill.

asr-000995
01:30:35.030 --> 01:30:49.390
Rep. Arnan C. Panaligan: I would suspect that the PD-415, I think it was because of the fact that we are under IMF control at that time

asr-000996
01:30:50.133 --> 01:30:53.200
Rep. Arnan C. Panaligan: with currency stabilization loans.

asr-000997
01:30:53.200 --> 01:30:55.280
Rep. Arnan C. Panaligan: That was in the 70s.

asr-000998
01:30:55.718 --> 01:31:04.400
Rep. Arnan C. Panaligan: So, that was the major imposition probably of the IMF that expenditures on foreign loans

asr-000999
01:31:04.400 --> 01:31:09.599
Rep. Arnan C. Panaligan: because of foreign exchange controls at that time should be limited to 300 million U.S. dollars

asr-001000
01:31:09.599 --> 01:31:18.027
Rep. Arnan C. Panaligan: in consideration for the grant of currency stabilization loans by the IMF.

asr-001001
01:31:18.787 --> 01:31:21.503
Rep. Arnan C. Panaligan: That is what I suspect, Your Honor.

asr-001002
01:31:23.174 --> 01:31:24.630
Rep. Arnan C. Panaligan: So, maybe we can now...

asr-001003
01:31:24.639 --> 01:31:25.351
Rep. Arnan C. Panaligan: Remove that cap.

asr-001004
01:31:25.621 --> 01:31:29.249
Rep. Arnan C. Panaligan: Anyway, I have here a copy of the U.S. Senate bill 1497 entitled

asr-001005
01:31:29.654 --> 01:31:33.856
Rep. Arnan C. Panaligan: A Bill to Modernize the Defense Capabilities of the Philippines and for Other Purposes.

asr-001006
01:31:33.974 --> 01:31:38.446
Rep. Arnan C. Panaligan: Do you have any information if this Senate bill in the U.S. has been enacted already?

asr-001007
01:31:39.863 --> 01:31:41.585
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: What Senate bill, Your Honor?

asr-001008
01:31:42.023 --> 01:31:45.854
Rep. Arnan C. Panaligan: Senate bill 1497 or the PERA, Philippine Enhanced Resiliency Act.

asr-001009
01:31:45.854 --> 01:31:50.880
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: It has been enacted, Your Honor, by the U.S. Congress.

asr-001010
01:31:50.880 --> 01:31:54.800
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Nonetheless, the funding, I believe, for next year will be...

asr-001011
01:31:54.800 --> 01:31:56.300
Rep. Arnan C. Panaligan: I thought 100 million U.S.

asr-001012
01:31:56.300 --> 01:32:00.502
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: 100 million that will be allocated by the U.S. government for it.

asr-001013
01:32:01.379 --> 01:32:09.023
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: It sets a maximum of 500 million U.S. dollars per year depending on the Treasury availability.

asr-001014
01:32:09.023 --> 01:32:17.360
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: And according to this law, the priority, coastal defense, long-range fires, maritime security, integrated air defense.

asr-001015
01:32:17.360 --> 01:32:23.148
Rep. Arnan C. Panaligan: So, I know that this will not be transferred to our Treasury because it's in the nature of a foreign military financing.

asr-001017
01:32:23.485 --> 01:32:31.788
Rep. Arnan C. Panaligan: But do you agree that this will help boost our modernization program and help solve the budgetary constraint problem?

asr-001018
01:32:31.973 --> 01:32:40.158
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: It will help, and together with the official security assistance that Japan gives us for domain awareness, Your Honor.

asr-001019
01:32:40.816 --> 01:32:46.030
Rep. Arnan C. Panaligan: Maybe DBM knows about this. That's the reason why they don't give you much allocation for modernization fund.

asr-001020
01:32:46.030 --> 01:32:53.455
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: No, Your Honor. Probably, it's really the fiscal consideration of the country on a macro level.

asr-001021
01:32:54.805 --> 01:33:04.981
Rep. Arnan C. Panaligan: So, then, it was reported in the Korean media in the past months that the Navy plans to acquire two more Malvar-class missile frigates.

asr-001022
01:33:05.487 --> 01:33:13.553
Rep. Arnan C. Panaligan: In addition, the two frigates ordered last year, so that would be the fifth and sixth guided missile frigate of the Navy.

asr-001023
01:33:13.942 --> 01:33:17.384
Rep. Arnan C. Panaligan: Are you at liberty to confirm this proposal?

asr-001024
01:33:19.004 --> 01:33:23.360
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Definitely, Your Honor. There is an intent, really, to acquire.

asr-001025
01:33:23.360 --> 01:33:25.788
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: The trigger has not yet been pulled.

asr-001026
01:33:28.471 --> 01:33:35.794
Rep. Arnan C. Panaligan: And also, every budget hearing, I make this follow-up regarding the upgrading and the completion,

asr-001027
01:33:35.795 --> 01:33:44.266
Rep. Arnan C. Panaligan: the installation of the still-unfitted sensors and weapon system for the Rizal-class and Malvar-class.

asr-001028
01:33:45.076 --> 01:33:46.038
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Your Honor, they are ongoing.

asr-001029
01:33:46.038 --> 01:33:48.552
Rep. Arnan C. Panaligan: Thank you. Thank you.

asr-001030
01:33:48.974 --> 01:33:54.796
Rep. Arnan C. Panaligan: So, also, some people ask me to relate this to you.

asr-001031
01:33:55.235 --> 01:33:56.000
Rep. Arnan C. Panaligan: How about the plan?

asr-001032
01:33:56.000 --> 01:34:00.044
Rep. Arnan C. Panaligan: As for the acquisition of multi-role fighters, I know that this is a very complicated matter.

asr-001033
01:34:00.415 --> 01:34:03.031
Rep. Arnan C. Panaligan: And for additional air defense missiles.

asr-001034
01:34:04.988 --> 01:34:06.828
Rep. Arnan C. Panaligan: And also, coastal defense missiles.

asr-001035
01:34:06.828 --> 01:34:11.440
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: It's still there, Your Honor, depending on the financing that we need.

asr-001036
01:34:11.440 --> 01:34:22.724
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: But now, knowing what we know, we have to have a lot of systems in place before any multi-role fighter is acquired.

asr-001037
01:34:23.753 --> 01:34:25.119
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Because a multi-role fighter...

asr-001038
01:34:25.119 --> 01:34:34.158
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: A multi-role fighter, as we saw recently, is heavily dependent on ground control and domain awareness.

asr-001039
01:34:34.159 --> 01:34:45.809
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: If not, it will be an unguided pilot-controlled aircraft, and its use will be marginal.

asr-001041
01:34:47.463 --> 01:34:55.529
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: So, maybe it's, Your Honor, without an air-to-air refueling, it will not be able to take off with adequate stores.

asr-001042
01:34:56.542 --> 01:35:08.388
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: And if we do not have the adequate hangarage facilities to service it, it will be useless, Your Honor.

asr-001043
01:35:09.704 --> 01:35:11.520
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: So, it comes as a force package.

asr-001044
01:35:11.520 --> 01:35:23.153
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: And as we learned, the minimum force package is 40 at any one mission, actually, for external defense.

asr-001045
01:35:24.571 --> 01:35:27.794
Rep. Arnan C. Panaligan: So, maybe, really, the amendment of PD 415 can help.

asr-001046
01:35:28.115 --> 01:35:30.400
Rep. Arnan C. Panaligan: It can help in obtaining funding for your programs.

asr-001047
01:35:30.400 --> 01:35:36.551
Rep. Arnan C. Panaligan: So, finally, Madam Chair, the Secretary, of course, is aware that it is the Executive Department

asr-001048
01:35:36.552 --> 01:35:43.319
Rep. Arnan C. Panaligan: that prepared this program of expenditures under the Constitution, not the Congress.

asr-001049
01:35:43.977 --> 01:35:49.833
Rep. Arnan C. Panaligan: And Congress has no power to increase the appropriations proposed by the President.

asr-001050
01:35:50.204 --> 01:35:57.241
Rep. Arnan C. Panaligan: We can do that, but we will get it from other items, which is very difficult on the part of Congress to do.

asr-001051
01:35:57.578 --> 01:36:04.717
Rep. Arnan C. Panaligan: So, the real battle here is at the level of the DBCC, the DBM, not here in Congress.

asr-001052
01:36:05.307 --> 01:36:12.400
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: I believe the connectivity and infrastructure are also necessary, Your Honor, for us to perform our mission roles.

asr-001053
01:36:12.400 --> 01:36:18.960
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: So, if the infrastructure budget will support the weight, really, of the equipment we need,

asr-001054
01:36:19.040 --> 01:36:21.946
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: it will solve a lot of our problems, too, on logistics.

asr-001055
01:36:22.857 --> 01:36:27.430
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: And I think that's the emphasis.

asr-001056
01:36:27.440 --> 01:36:28.865
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Of course, on education, too.

asr-001057
01:36:30.012 --> 01:36:33.016
Rep. Arnan C. Panaligan: And Madam Chair, no more questions.

asr-001058
01:36:33.472 --> 01:36:41.453
Rep. Arnan C. Panaligan: But in spite of budgetary constraints, our AFP and DND, they are doing their best to secure our territory and our sovereignty.

asr-001059
01:36:41.605 --> 01:36:47.519
Rep. Arnan C. Panaligan: So, on behalf of the people of my district, let me extend my sincerest appreciation to them.

asr-001060
01:36:47.520 --> 01:36:49.503
Rep. Arnan C. Panaligan: Thank you for your service to our officers and men.

asr-001061
01:36:50.988 --> 01:36:52.540
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Thank you, Congressman Panaligan.

asr-001062
01:36:53.654 --> 01:36:57.299
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Next to interpolate, Congressman Arlyn Ayon from the minority.

asr-001063
01:36:59.341 --> 01:37:01.501
Rep. Arlyn P. Ayon: Thank you, Madam Chair.

asr-001064
01:37:01.920 --> 01:37:10.550
Rep. Arlyn P. Ayon: Good morning, Mr. Secretary, to our distinguished members of the committee, our officers and men of the Armed Forces of the Philippines,

asr-001065
01:37:10.560 --> 01:37:13.702
Rep. Arlyn P. Ayon: and all the officials and guests present here today.

asr-001066
01:37:14.719 --> 01:37:23.236
Rep. Arlyn P. Ayon: First, I would like to express my appreciation to you, Mr. Secretary, for your leadership and for the various initiatives you have undertaken

asr-001067
01:37:24.560 --> 01:37:25.670
Rep. Arlyn P. Ayon: to strengthen our national defense.

asr-001068
01:37:25.680 --> 01:37:26.600
Rep. Arlyn P. Ayon: Thank you, Mr. Secretary.

asr-001071
01:37:26.639 --> 01:37:30.695
Rep. Arlyn P. Ayon: I am one of those who strongly support the Department of National Defense.

asr-001072
01:37:31.679 --> 01:37:36.550
Rep. Arlyn P. Ayon: Coming from Bukidnon, a province that has experienced the reality of insurgency,

asr-001073
01:37:36.560 --> 01:37:42.760
Rep. Arlyn P. Ayon: I have personally witnessed how our gallant men and women of the Armed Forces of the Philippines

asr-001074
01:37:43.520 --> 01:37:49.527
Rep. Arlyn P. Ayon: have courageously protected our communities and our nation.

asr-001075
01:37:50.320 --> 01:37:57.340
Rep. Arlyn P. Ayon: Today, we are very happy to share that Bukidnon has become one of our country's emerging tourist destination.

asr-001076
01:37:57.920 --> 01:38:07.109
Rep. Arlyn P. Ayon: And I believe that this progress has been made possible in large part because of the stable peace and security that our province now enjoys.

asr-001077
01:38:07.119 --> 01:38:15.669
Rep. Arlyn P. Ayon: Our active soldiers have contributed tremendously, not only for our national security, but also to our economic and national development.

asr-001078
01:38:15.679 --> 01:38:25.669
Rep. Arlyn P. Ayon: But, Mr. Secretary, I would also like to take this opportunity to highlight our veterans, both our uniformed personnel and the civilian human resources

asr-001079
01:38:25.679 --> 01:38:29.690
Rep. Arlyn P. Ayon: who have devoted many years to the defense of our country.

asr-001080
01:38:39.920 --> 01:38:49.265
Rep. Arlyn P. Ayon: I believe that we must never forget that these heroes who once carried the burden of protecting our nation.

asr-001081
01:38:49.760 --> 01:38:56.550
Rep. Arlyn P. Ayon: May I therefore ask, Mr. Secretary, in the Department's plans and budget priorities,

asr-001082
01:38:56.560 --> 01:39:02.870
Rep. Arlyn P. Ayon: have we given equal weight and importance to the welfare of our veterans throughout the country,

asr-001083
01:39:02.880 --> 01:39:09.590
Rep. Arlyn P. Ayon: particularly those who are now elderly and facing increasing health care and living expenses?

asr-001084
01:39:09.600 --> 01:39:17.750
Rep. Arlyn P. Ayon: And finally, how can we as lawmakers work together with the Department to properly honor these heroes,

asr-001085
01:39:17.760 --> 01:39:24.709
Rep. Arlyn P. Ayon: not merely through words of gratitude, but through concrete programs, adequate benefits, health care,

asr-001086
01:39:24.719 --> 01:39:34.034
Rep. Arlyn P. Ayon: and support for those who are suffering from illnesses and long-term effects of the stress, trauma, and sacrifices they endured in the service of our nation?

asr-001087
01:39:34.800 --> 01:39:43.830
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Thank you very much to the distinguished colleague, former distinguished member of the House.

asr-001088
01:39:43.840 --> 01:39:50.032
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: I believe that it's well appropriate that you raise the issue.

asr-001089
01:39:50.560 --> 01:39:55.246
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: And I think what we should do, really, is to decouple.

asr-001090
01:39:58.080 --> 01:40:04.358
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: We should decouple the veterans' pensions from active duty salaries.

asr-001091
01:40:04.800 --> 01:40:15.580
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: So we can adjust their pensions without adjusting necessarily the pay increases for our active duty personnel.

asr-001092
01:40:16.159 --> 01:40:25.040
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Actually, the recent increases in pay were due to a compromise we reached with the

asr-001094
01:40:25.040 --> 01:40:34.717
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: veterans to increase their pension rates 5% for three years, in total 15% by 2028.

asr-001095
01:40:35.760 --> 01:40:48.402
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: But unless the increases are decoupled by law from the active duty rates,

asr-001096
01:40:50.320 --> 01:40:54.865
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: you need to increase the rates of the active duty personnel.

asr-001097
01:40:57.440 --> 01:41:00.950
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Secondly, Your Honor, we are trying really to reach out to them.

asr-001098
01:41:00.960 --> 01:41:13.175
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: And we still are hopefully going to be able to launch our first hospice hopefully by the end of the year

asr-001099
01:41:15.040 --> 01:41:19.958
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: for taking care of the older veterans who have no place to call home

asr-001100
01:41:21.119 --> 01:41:25.105
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: and who are forced to be confined in hospitals.

asr-001101
01:41:25.520 --> 01:41:27.417
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Because there's nowhere else to go.

asr-001102
01:41:27.600 --> 01:41:34.709
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Our issue there is the accreditation of the caregivers and the finding of caregivers

asr-001103
01:41:34.719 --> 01:41:36.563
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: and the building of the facility.

asr-001104
01:41:38.320 --> 01:41:43.178
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Nonetheless, we have to get our feet wet with it in order to provide them adequate

asr-001105
01:41:46.000 --> 01:41:49.709
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: a place where they can retire with dignity.

asr-001106
01:41:51.360 --> 01:41:55.189
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Thirdly, Your Honor, it's knowing fully well that

asr-001107
01:41:55.199 --> 01:42:11.680
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: the veterans need to adequate socialization, if not some of them confined to home really suffer.

asr-001108
01:42:12.239 --> 01:42:22.709
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: And I've seen it with even younger veterans who were very active before but when withdrawn from their comfort zone,

asr-001109
01:42:22.719 --> 01:42:24.961
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: so to speak, have become.

asr-001110
01:42:26.320 --> 01:42:32.521
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Have become, you know, very withdrawn and their families talk to me about it.

asr-001111
01:42:34.480 --> 01:42:38.984
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Fourthly, Your Honor, a lot of the predicament of veterans in terms of health

asr-001112
01:42:39.600 --> 01:42:43.405
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: can be addressed preventively while they are still in active duty.

asr-001113
01:42:44.639 --> 01:42:53.340
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: That's why the active duty care right now, when we are seeing the onset of diseases like heart disease,

asr-001114
01:42:53.350 --> 01:42:55.160
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: diabetes,

asr-001115
01:42:55.199 --> 01:42:58.550
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: heart attacks at a younger age, right now at 35,

asr-001116
01:42:58.560 --> 01:43:04.820
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: we've seen a lot of people really get affected by strokes.

asr-001117
01:43:06.560 --> 01:43:14.742
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: So we'll have to be more proactive in monitoring the diseases

asr-001118
01:43:15.199 --> 01:43:23.510
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: which may exacerbate their situation when they become veterans and require extensive care,

asr-001119
01:43:23.520 --> 01:43:24.650
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: which could have been prevented.

asr-001120
01:43:24.660 --> 01:43:27.240
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: So it's not a big deal for us to do that.

asr-001121
01:43:27.280 --> 01:43:29.109
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: But it is a big problem and it's not something that is perfectly anticipated

asr-001122
01:43:29.119 --> 01:43:31.617
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: had we known of the situation beforehand.

asr-001123
01:43:34.400 --> 01:43:40.544
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: So, Your Honor, I think on the pension system, while not opposed to pension reform,

asr-001124
01:43:42.239 --> 01:43:47.497
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: I think the key there is not to lump the AFP retirees with the others.

asr-001125
01:43:48.960 --> 01:43:54.398
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: I know it's kind of controversial, but the AFP is a national force that is part of the national system.

asr-001126
01:43:56.239 --> 01:44:00.929
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: receives no subsidies from any other agency.

asr-001127
01:44:01.760 --> 01:44:05.189
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Unlike, let's say, the BFP or the PNP,

asr-001128
01:44:05.199 --> 01:44:13.754
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: they have more roles with the local communities that they are there to serve.

asr-001129
01:44:15.119 --> 01:44:21.990
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: And so the basis of the pension on the basis of fairness should be segregated

asr-001130
01:44:22.000 --> 01:44:30.390
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: and agencies or communities which derive benefits from directed or targeted services

asr-001131
01:44:30.400 --> 01:44:34.207
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: like PJMP or PNP should share in the pension burden.

asr-001132
01:44:34.880 --> 01:44:38.662
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Unlike the AFP, which is a purely sovereign and national force.

asr-001133
01:44:41.760 --> 01:44:49.580
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: I realize, really, that there will come a time when pensions, if not reformed now,

asr-001134
01:44:52.400 --> 01:44:53.444
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: will be more important.

asr-001135
01:44:54.320 --> 01:44:55.510
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Will eat up.

asr-001136
01:44:55.520 --> 01:44:57.910
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: will eat up a lot of fiscal space.

asr-001137
01:44:57.920 --> 01:45:04.470
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Nonetheless, if at this day and age,

asr-001138
01:45:04.480 --> 01:45:07.510
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: at this stage of our national development

asr-001139
01:45:07.520 --> 01:45:12.293
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: where the AFP is fully engaged with the law troop ceiling

asr-001140
01:45:12.880 --> 01:45:17.086
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: on several mission areas 365 days of the year,

asr-001141
01:45:18.080 --> 01:45:22.199
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: I think they need the peace of mind.

asr-001142
01:45:23.199 --> 01:45:27.910
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: And since the retirees also form part of the AFP family

asr-001143
01:45:27.920 --> 01:45:33.134
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: who are there helping each and every step of the way,

asr-001144
01:45:35.920 --> 01:45:40.790
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: I think at this stage, it's best the pension be studied

asr-001145
01:45:40.800 --> 01:45:47.039
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: unlike the old RSPS system which was not a sustainable system.

asr-001146
01:45:50.080 --> 01:45:51.830
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: And until we are...

asr-001147
01:45:51.840 --> 01:45:55.910
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: We are sure that there is a full-proof system

asr-001148
01:45:55.920 --> 01:46:01.669
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: which will guarantee them peace of mind when they retire

asr-001149
01:46:01.679 --> 01:46:06.125
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: and which will motivate them to commit themselves.

asr-001150
01:46:07.679 --> 01:46:11.575
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: And if not the same way, perhaps even a greater way

asr-001151
01:46:12.000 --> 01:46:13.482
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: to mission accomplishment,

asr-001152
01:46:15.520 --> 01:46:19.850
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: then I think it's best to err on the side of giving peace of mind

asr-001153
01:46:19.860 --> 01:46:20.920
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: to our activities.

asr-001154
01:46:20.960 --> 01:46:27.539
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: To our duty personnel and our veterans.

asr-001155
01:46:28.480 --> 01:46:30.470
Rep. Arlyn P. Ayon: Thank you for that, Mr. Secretary.

asr-001156
01:46:30.480 --> 01:46:31.430
Rep. Arlyn P. Ayon: That's our concern.

asr-001157
01:46:31.440 --> 01:46:36.950
Rep. Arlyn P. Ayon: So hopefully, and can BND assure this committee

asr-001158
01:46:36.960 --> 01:46:40.870
Rep. Arlyn P. Ayon: that no Filipino veterans who serve our country honorably

asr-001159
01:46:40.880 --> 01:46:43.430
Rep. Arlyn P. Ayon: will be left behind because of lack of funds,

asr-001160
01:46:43.440 --> 01:46:46.372
Rep. Arlyn P. Ayon: delayed benefits, or inadequate health care?

asr-001161
01:46:48.239 --> 01:46:52.149
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Rest assured, we are at the forefront of fighting for veterans' benefits.

asr-001162
01:46:52.159 --> 01:46:58.070
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: And my personal connection with our close relationship

asr-001163
01:46:58.080 --> 01:47:00.550
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: with veterans' groups of whatever sort,

asr-001164
01:47:00.560 --> 01:47:03.854
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: and particularly even our retired enlisted personnel

asr-001165
01:47:04.719 --> 01:47:08.870
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: and our retired NCOs and civilian personnel

asr-001166
01:47:08.880 --> 01:47:13.017
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: because they develop a lot of expertise.

asr-001167
01:47:15.280 --> 01:47:19.497
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Post-retirement, actually, we still try to use them as best as we can.

asr-001168
01:47:21.679 --> 01:47:22.470
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Keeping them occupied.

asr-001169
01:47:22.480 --> 01:47:27.189
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: At the same time, while training the next generation

asr-001170
01:47:27.199 --> 01:47:32.018
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: of people who will succeed in leadership positions, particularly.

asr-001171
01:47:32.719 --> 01:47:33.590
Rep. Arlyn P. Ayon: Thank you, Mr. Secretary.

asr-001172
01:47:33.600 --> 01:47:35.590
Rep. Arlyn P. Ayon: That will be all, Madam Chairman.

asr-001173
01:47:35.600 --> 01:47:35.950
Rep. Arlyn P. Ayon: Thank you.

asr-001174
01:47:36.159 --> 01:47:36.794
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Thank you to the other.

asr-001175
01:47:37.679 --> 01:47:39.528
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Thank you, Congressman Ayon.

asr-001176
01:47:40.320 --> 01:47:45.873
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Next interpellate, Congressman Munir Erbison from the majority.

asr-001177
01:47:49.720 --> 01:47:53.540
Rep. Munir N. Arbison Jr.: Magandang umaga, Madam Chairman.

asr-001179
01:47:54.640 --> 01:47:57.040
Rep. Munir N. Arbison Jr.: Magandang umaga sa lahat.

asr-001180
01:48:00.080 --> 01:48:02.180
Rep. Munir N. Arbison Jr.: Just want to make a manifestation.

asr-001181
01:48:04.620 --> 01:48:09.540
Rep. Munir N. Arbison Jr.: I would like to express my full support for the Department of National Defense

asr-001182
01:48:10.280 --> 01:48:14.520
Rep. Munir N. Arbison Jr.: and recognize its important role in maintaining peace and security

asr-001183
01:48:14.520 --> 01:48:15.880
Rep. Munir N. Arbison Jr.: in the 2nd District of Sulu.

asr-001184
01:48:15.880 --> 01:48:20.020
Rep. Munir N. Arbison Jr.: We are grateful to the DND and the Armed Forces of the Philippines

asr-001185
01:48:20.020 --> 01:48:24.460
Rep. Munir N. Arbison Jr.: for their continued presence and support.

asr-001186
01:48:24.460 --> 01:48:29.360
Rep. Munir N. Arbison Jr.: In our communities, their efforts have helped us sustain peace

asr-001187
01:48:29.360 --> 01:48:37.420
Rep. Munir N. Arbison Jr.: and create a better environment for the development of the province of Sulu.

asr-001188
01:48:37.580 --> 01:48:42.880
Rep. Munir N. Arbison Jr.: We hope for their continued support as we work together to preserve peace

asr-001189
01:48:42.880 --> 01:48:45.440
Rep. Munir N. Arbison Jr.: and progress we have achieved.

asr-001190
01:48:45.880 --> 01:48:51.940
Rep. Munir N. Arbison Jr.: Dati-dati, ang tinatanong ng mga kababayan natin,

asr-001191
01:48:52.040 --> 01:48:54.180
Rep. Munir N. Arbison Jr.: Kumusta ng Sulu?

asr-001192
01:48:54.360 --> 01:48:56.600
Rep. Munir N. Arbison Jr.: Ang daming sabi niya mga problema.

asr-001193
01:48:57.180 --> 01:49:03.700
Rep. Munir N. Arbison Jr.: Pero ngayon, ang tinatanong kung anong magandang beach sa Sulu kasi peaceful.

asr-001194
01:49:04.000 --> 01:49:04.840
Rep. Munir N. Arbison Jr.: Maraming salamat.

asr-001195
01:49:06.980 --> 01:49:10.380
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Papasalamat po ako, magsukul, sa ating kapatid na taga-Sulu.

asr-001196
01:49:11.760 --> 01:49:15.320
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Malaki pong tulong sa atin ang katahimikan sa Sulu.

asr-001197
01:49:15.320 --> 01:49:22.620
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: At iyan po ay magbibigay po ng oportunidad sa ating WestMinCom.

asr-001198
01:49:23.300 --> 01:49:26.300
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Lalo na ang Naval Forces West.

asr-001199
01:49:27.180 --> 01:49:41.240
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Na mag-perform po ng functions to guard the Sulu Sea passage na papasok

asr-001200
01:49:41.820 --> 01:49:49.780
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: sa ating major sea lane or international sea lane of communication sa internal waters po natin.

asr-001201
01:49:50.040 --> 01:49:56.360
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: So marami pong salamat sa dati kong classmate, si Congressman Arbison,

asr-001202
01:49:56.560 --> 01:50:03.460
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: sa katahimikan, sa Sulu, at hope to see you soon.

asr-001203
01:50:08.000 --> 01:50:10.520
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Thank you. Thank you, Congressman Munir Arbison.

asr-001204
01:50:12.480 --> 01:50:16.080
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Next to interpellate from the minority, Congressman Antonio Tinio.

asr-001205
01:50:20.300 --> 01:51:32.700
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Salamat, Chair. Meron pong powerpoint kung pwede. Pero tutuloy ko na habang hihintay natin. Una yung tungkol pa rin sa pension reform, MUP pension reform. Nung 2015 ang budget para sa MUP pension was 68.6 billion. Ngayong 2027, the proposed budget for pension is 154 billion. So mahigit nag-doble na po. Nag-discuss na kanina pero sumasang-ayon po ba ang DND na urgent. Kailangan na pong mapatupad yung pag-reforma. At ang pinaka-reforma na kailangan ay kailangan magkaroon na ng contribution system ang AFP at uniformed personnel, katulad nung ibang mga government employees at saka private na nagkocontribute sa SSS, may counterpart, at doon ang gagaling ang pensyon. Hindi yung kasalukuyan na buong-buo na sinasubsidized ng GAA.

asr-001217
01:51:32.700 --> 01:53:41.620
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Ito po ang aking kasagutan. Yung 154 po, katulad nung naipaliwanag dating kanina, 49% lang po doon ang nasa AFP. Umakyat po dahil humingi po ang ating mga veterano ng adjustment. Dahil wala pong adjustment for the past years. Ako po hindi po tutol sa pension reform, lamang kung papaano ito ma-implement. Kailangan po pag-aaralan natin ang efekto ng engganyo na sumama po sa serbisyo. And actually, yung risk po na hinaharap na pwede pong lalong-lalo na po yung mga totally disabled na bata, yun po ang talagang malaki. Kasi automatic discharge po na magkakaroon siya ng benefits based on his current rank. So hindi po ako tutol kahit nasa contributions but when will we start it and who will be affected. So it has to be studied. And the most important thing po is to separate the armed forces from the rest of the civilian agencies. Katulad po ng PNP at saka BJMP, part of the service is local or a major part. So it's also fair that the LGUs share the pension burden. Ngayon po, yung disposable income po nila naiiwan din sa pamilya. Hindi wala po akong debate yung mga teacher natin. Malaki din po ang risk. Lalo-lalo na nakikita po natin yung teacher na tumatawid sa baha para pumunta lang sa eskwelahan. Ngunit ang pakiusap lang, pag-aaralan po itong mabuti at kung kailan po i-implement.

asr-001236
01:53:44.500 --> 01:54:31.300
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So, Chair, pakalawang beses binanggit ni Secretary yung pangangailangan ihiwalay yung pension ng military sa civilian uniform. I suppose. So, yun yung police, BJMP, Bucor, etc. At ang kuha ko sa sinasabi nyo, dapat may contribution din ng LGU sa kanilang pensyon. Could you elaborate on this? Parang ngayon ko lang narinig ang ganitong proposal. Parang sinasabi, ngayon, national government ang buong-buong nagbabayad ng pensyon. So, ang sinasuggest nyo ba dapat kalgahinan ng LGU? At least a part of it? Of the civilian uniform personnel pension?

asr-001245
01:54:31.300 --> 01:55:14.500
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Opo, dapat pag-aaralan po natin. Hindi ko po sinasabi that is one way. Pero kailangan po i-examine po natin dahil ang servisyo ng police is basically local, no? Except for national crime-fighting authorities. So, in terms of burden sharing, dahil yung era po, alam naman po natin that that goes in block, which is undiminished. I think we might want to study the fiscal impact of burden sharing for them. I'm not saying that that's a cut-and-dried solution. Pero tingnan po natin para naman ma-ease yung pension burden ng ating national government.

asr-001252
01:55:16.560 --> 01:55:31.280
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay. Ngayon ko lang narinig ito na burden sharing ang ibig sabihin ipakarga yung pensyon ng police. At iba pang uniform aside from military sa LGU. Pero...

asr-001255
01:55:32.440 --> 01:55:51.920
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Hindi po totally. Marami pong financial permutations na puwedeng mangyari on an actuarial basis. So importante din po talaga itong pag-aralan on an actuarial and sustainable basis.

asr-001259
01:55:53.400 --> 01:55:57.100
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Pero ang basic po doon: sa ngayon, kayo, dapat may contribution?

asr-001261
01:55:58.500 --> 01:56:22.300
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: It depends po on when and how. Sa ngayon po, nakatutok po at punong-puno ngayon yung ating sundalo dahil halos 90% na yung fill-up. Hindi po ako, in conscience, puwedeng humingi sa kanila ng contribution sa ngayon. And we are requiring them to do more, insofar as I'm concerned.

asr-001273
01:56:22.700 --> 01:56:29.440
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So kayo, sa ngayon, tingin ninyo hindi dapat hingan ng contribution?

asr-001276
01:56:29.440 --> 01:56:54.700
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Hindi po dapat. Tingnan po natin kung may sustainable na programa na kakayanin naman po nila at patas po sa kanila; we will consider it. We will be open to it. All proposals for easing the fiscal burden are open, but there are no definitives until we see the plan.

asr-001290
01:56:56.400 --> 01:57:31.660
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Hindi po bago yung mga proposals for pension reform. I mean, sa totoo lang, nung una akong pumasok sa Kongreso, pinag-uusapan na po ito. I would imagine, nung nasa Kongreso pa kayo, issue na rin ito. At isa sa mga proposal doon po doon na yung mga bagong papasok, sa kanila ipapatupad yung contribution system. Ibig sabihin, yung mga nasa servisyo na, pwedeng hindi na. Sabi nyo nga, parang may kontrata yan, nung pumasok sila, kailangang i-fulfill yun. Pero sa mga bago, hindi ba pwedeng ganon?

asr-001307
01:57:32.200 --> 01:58:34.900
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Actually po, that would make sense because then you have time for the pension plan to mature. So that, may drawdown. Pag unang drawdown po doon sa pension system na iyon, yung mga nag-contribute na magbe-benefit. So i-carry na lang yung mga [unclear]. Siyempre, maaari din po iyon. Iyon nga lang, pag-aralan lang po natin yung optional at mandatory retirements kasi baka naman po maubos yung optional at makaapekto din yung pension sa kung magkano ang sahod. Depende na po sa actuarial. Lalo-lalo na po kung may legislated benefits. Iyon po ang problema. Iyon po ang kakain sa buhay ng pondo. But, you know, sa bagong entry po na mag-contribution, and then if you can design a pension system that will benefit them to allow the system to mature, why not? We can consider it all.

asr-001339
01:58:34.900 --> 01:58:58.080
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay. May baka tanong pa, pero let me move on to another issue. Recently, the Secretary made statements regarding Chinese language teaching and cultural exchange sa mga Filipino-Chinese schools dito sa Pilipinas. Could you elaborate on your concern regarding this?

asr-001351
01:58:58.080 --> 02:00:02.660
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: It was a matter of concern, Your Honor, because it was reported that the training was done by Jinan University. And Jinan University was the source of the supposed study that Batanes was part of China. And we all know, Your Honor, that this is a state university, and depending on how you look at things, I think if it's state-sponsored, then you mean party-sponsored. And so, it is a matter of concern that even as a normal parent, that Chinese language teachers who may even be teaching minors are coming from the same institution that published these kinds of supposed academic studies. It's a matter of concern, but our agency has alerted other agencies, and we're not actively pursuing anything on it.

asr-001380
02:00:03.740 --> 02:00:40.080
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Mayroon po kayong statement sa isang Kapihan sa Manila Bay Forum. Sabi ninyo rito na malaking ebidensya na itong mga eskwelahan ay ginagamit sa malign influence. Ang tinutukoy ninyo po ay yung mga local Filipino-Chinese schools. Hindi naman lahat, pero mayroon diyang malign influence. Kaya dapat maging masusi tayo, hindi lamang sa university kundi sa mga mababang paaralan kung saan may cultural and language and other exchanges. Sabi ninyo po may ebidensya, malaking ebidensya na may mga eskwelahan.

asr-001387
02:00:40.080 --> 02:00:49.620
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: It's res ipsa loquitur on their part. If they publish something, I was referring to the university, Jinan.

asr-001389
02:00:50.060 --> 02:00:56.880
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So ang tinutukoy ninyo po rito ay yung university, hindi yung mga school. I-clarify po natin kasi very sensitive po ito.

asr-001391
02:00:57.000 --> 02:01:03.540
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Yes, I beg to clarify. Thank the gentleman for asking the clarification. It's [unclear] University because...

asr-001393
02:01:03.540 --> 02:01:05.920
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: So hindi ninyo po tinutukoy yung mga local Chinese schools?

asr-001394
02:01:06.180 --> 02:01:07.140
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: We have no evidence.

asr-001395
02:01:07.220 --> 02:01:08.280
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: You have no evidence?

asr-001396
02:01:08.580 --> 02:01:09.060
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Yes, Your Honor.

asr-001397
02:01:09.060 --> 02:01:14.200
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay, thank you for that clarification. Kasi nga po, parang ang... We don't want to cause panic.

asr-001399
02:01:14.200 --> 02:01:15.060
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Yes, Your Honor.

asr-001400
02:01:15.060 --> 02:01:18.240
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Yes, especially among the Filipino-Chinese community.

asr-001402
02:01:19.260 --> 02:02:16.600
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Okay. Now, of course, sangayon tayo na talagang kabalbalan yung claim nung Jinan University na ang Batanes ay bahagi ng Pilipinas. Pero itong... Let me wind up, Madam Chair. Itong issue na to ay nagmula sa isang report ng SeaLight. Ayan po, that is the report. The university that said batanes is China is also training Manila's Chinese teachers. Okay. This is an article published by Juan Ray Powell, the director of SeaLight. Ngayon, itong SeaLight po, are you aware of the funding and the origins of SeaLight?

asr-001409
02:02:16.660 --> 02:02:19.620
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: I'm not aware of the funding, Your Honor, but I know the individual.

asr-001410
02:02:20.060 --> 02:02:21.000
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Si Ray Powell?

asr-001411
02:02:21.000 --> 02:02:21.740
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Yes, Your Honor.

asr-001412
02:02:21.880 --> 02:02:55.460
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Of course. Si Ray Powell, of course, is actually laman ng balita yan, lumalabas sa media often, and he talks about these issues. Now, next slide po. Actually, yung kanyang SeaLight, you are... I don't know, maybe... Ito ang lumalabas po, na yung kanyang SeaLight is a project of the Gordian Knot Center for... The Gordian Knot Center for Strategic Innovation. Tama po. Is that correct?

asr-001418
02:02:55.480 --> 02:02:58.000
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: I'm not in a position to confirm or deny, Your Honor.

asr-001419
02:02:58.010 --> 02:05:16.640
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Next slide po. Yung Gordian Knot Center for... Sorry, it's called Stanford University's Gordian Knot Center for National Security Innovation. Okay. According to this article published on the navy.mil website, meaning to say U.S. Navy, website, this was established by the Office of Naval Research, which is a part of the U.S. Navy. So, next slide. And so, the director, ayan na po, the Office of Naval Research, which is part of the U.S. Navy. And, next slide. Yung kanyang Sea... This is the social media Twitter account of Ray Powell, and his handle is Gordian Knot Ray. Yun yung koneksyon. So, in other words, itong si Ray Powell, na aktibong-aktibo sa media ng Pilipinas, and in fact, sets the media agenda, dahil siya yung unang naglabas nung report regarding the Chinese University, apparently, ay, you know, nakaugnay pala sa U.S. Navy. Yung kanyang center ay tinatag ng U.S. Navy. So, hindi po ba maituturing din ito? In the same way na yung ginagawa ng China ay tinatawag na foreign information manipulation and interference, ay, di ba, pwede rin, dapat din ituring na foreign information manipulation, and interference, ang SeaLight at itong si Ray Powell. In other words, kailangan may disclosure din, at may transparency at disclosure sa pinanggagalingan ditong Ray Powell, at madalas na sina-cite ng DND, ng Coast Guard, si Admiral Tarriela, at iba pa.

asr-001440
02:05:16.640 --> 02:06:11.084
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: I think that that's up to him to address, Your Honor. For the Gordian Knot Center to address. For us, we have our own independent sources. Now, what's important here is what the information is. Is it accurate or not? When we compare a Batanes narrative with activities in the West Philippine Sea, the proof of the pudding is in the eating. And what we are after in foreign malign influence is misinformation. So, and, and, not information per se, it's misinformation. So, at the end of the day, the credibility will lie on who has the more accurate information. But in terms of his connections, that is for him to disclose.

asr-001451
02:06:11.160 --> 02:06:19.040
Rep. Antonio L. Tinio: Of course. Okay. So, agad ko na lang po yung tanong ko, pero meron pa akong mga tanong. So, next round na lang po. Thank you, Madam Chair.

asr-001453
02:06:19.220 --> 02:06:27.780
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Yes. Thank you. Thank you, Congressman Tinio. Next to interpolate from the majority, Representative Johanne Bautista.

asr-001456
02:06:28.100 --> 02:07:13.280
Rep. Johanne Monich G. Bautista: Thank you, Madam Chair. And good morning po to the members of the committee, my fellow colleagues, and of course, Secretary Teodoro and the DND family. Magandang umaga po sa inyong lahat. I will be asking questions po pertaining to our uniform personnel. I'm not sure if it's classified information. To ask, more or less, ilan po ba ang ating uniform personnel? And if that is classified information, may I ask, Madam Chair, magkano po ba sa pondo ng department ang allocated for the uniforms and fabrics of our uniform personnel, more or less, Madam Chair?

asr-001466
02:07:14.260 --> 02:07:42.720
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: For the uniform personnel, Your Honor, we have 162,000. As for the clothing, I'm not too sure. Your Honor, because we have to aggregate, the clothing is per service. We don't have the aggregated amount at this time. But we can provide you with the information.

asr-001471
02:07:43.500 --> 02:08:57.520
Rep. Johanne Monich G. Bautista: All right, Madam Chair. We can await that figures. The reason I'm asking this, Madam Chair, is that pertaining to RA 9242 or the Philippine Tropical Fabrics, this was passed in 2004, and this requires the use of Philippine Tropical Fabrics for government uniforms and to support locally manufactured products, local resources, and promote employment, no? This is for our local industries. Particularly po, yung IRR po niya, strengthened implementation by requiring local sourcing and the DOST PTRI testing and certification, and there are also allowed exemptions. In other words, it is not enough that our uniforms are made in the country, it is required that we use a certain amount of Philippine fabrics. So, may we ask kung wala man pong ano for the department, Madam Chair, to submit if they have projected figures on what would the budget to be spent on RA 9242 compliant Philippine-made fabrics. Madam Chair.

asr-001484
02:08:57.520 --> 02:09:56.060
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: I don't have the figure right now, Your Honor, because the fabric must not only be Philippine-made, but must conform to minimum standards of safety and fireproofing that we have. We know that an indigenous fabric industry is hard to get, because we don't have indigenous cotton and other fabrics which actually cannot be substituted based on the safety considerations. Nonetheless, Your Honor, we will provide you with the information, and it's not a question of the manufacturer, really. It's the sourcing of the fabric, and we have to resource fabric, actually, to more trusted sources, meaning to say countries which, if at all, are not involved in disputes with us.

asr-001494
02:09:57.180 --> 02:10:28.180
Rep. Johanne Monich G. Bautista: Thank you for that, Madam Chair and Mr. Secretary. Now, going to the issue of local sourcing, Madam Chair, if the Philippine manufacturers cannot yet supply all of the, or at least some of, the uniform requirements or meet certain military specifications, meron po bang ginagawa ang department together with the DOST, PTRI, and the local industry to at least address that gap and eventually comply with this law?

asr-001500
02:10:28.180 --> 02:11:18.320
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Thank you for the question, Your Honor. Honestly, I have not had the chance to devote time with the DOST and with the local fabric industry, because I'm really concerned now on our supply chains more than anything. So, it's something I'll schedule to look into it on a department-wide basis. But then, it will depend also on the production of, and the agricultural production that we have for cotton. And I know that for silk, for example, for parachutes, there were some who tried to venture into silk, but there was no market unless silk was branded with a country. So, the experiments failed.

asr-001510
02:11:19.760 --> 02:12:11.780
Rep. Johanne Monich G. Bautista: Thank you, Madam Chair. Actually, I think the IRR of the law that I'm mentioning, only requires 5% to use Philippine fabrics. And I believe that the Army, under former General Navarrete, I read somewhere that they actually started meeting with the DOST on the matter. Now, I think as regards the issue of local sourcing, it's just a suggestion and maybe the department can also help by providing maybe projected needs. In order for us to help develop our local industry for the fabrics. And at the same time, comply po with the requirement of using at least 5% of Philippine fabric for our uniforms, Madam Chair.

asr-001521
02:12:11.780 --> 02:12:33.180
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: I was informed to the Honorable Representative and Madam Chair that the issue there is our battle dress uniforms, which have safety standards. But for the general office attire, I think there is some component of Philippine fabrics and of course the office barongs.

asr-001527
02:12:35.360 --> 02:12:58.140
Rep. Johanne Monich G. Bautista: Yes, Madam Chair. Just to me, if we are able to communicate the needed requirements, standards, then hopefully maybe we can help develop or grow that industry and locally source our own products for the making of our uniforms, Madam Chair.

asr-001532
02:12:58.140 --> 02:13:45.340
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: I think, Your Honor, I will welcome the idea because locally made should not necessarily be locally grown, just as long as the growing is on a Philippine [unclear] country basis, like the experiment made with the beef industry before, where we had no grazing land and the original plan was to have a beef or cattle industry somewhere else where land was cheap and just imported for the Philippines. So we really have to be creative about these arrangements that we make, particularly if all our arable land is for food production rather than non-food items.

asr-001543
02:13:46.120 --> 02:14:40.220
Rep. Johanne Monich G. Bautista: Thank you, Madam Chair. I think that's a very valuable suggestion. We welcome it. Yes, Madam Chair and Mr. Secretary. And anyway, the requirement so far of the law is only 5% of the entire uniform, I think. Now, moving on, Madam Chair, under RA 12024 or the Self-Reliant Defense Posture Law, it directs the government to strengthen the local defense industry, support in-country enterprises, promote technology transfer, develop resilient supply chains, and prioritize local employment. For the 2027 budget, Madam Chair, can the Department provide us on how much procurement or program spending is expected to support local production, local maintenance, Filipino suppliers, more or less, Madam Chair?

asr-001559
02:14:40.940 --> 02:15:58.500
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: There will be, honestly speaking, none, Your Honor. Why? The law is fatally flawed. It does not provide for co-equity and co-investment, and it does not provide for research and development. So it will not meet the needs of a future armed force. So unless you put in the law provision for equity or research and development, there will be no right-thinking producer of technology that will allow you to benefit on the upside when you do not share the risk of the downside. That is a simple value proposition, Your Honor. Because the most important thing is not the production, even though 100% production is done outside. It's the intellectual property rights that are important, that you have equal rights to the IPR. That is the key and the cornerstone. If you cannot acquire the intellectual property rights, then you have no rights at all, even though you are co-producing. There will be no technology transfer. That's a value proposition that those who have been in the private sector know and know fully well.

asr-001597
02:15:59.840 --> 02:16:10.520
Rep. Johanne Monich G. Bautista: Thank you, Madam Chair and Mr. Secretary, for that very straightforward answer. And I think it is the position of the Secretary that there is a need to amend this law?

asr-001603
02:16:11.440 --> 02:16:38.040
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Definitely, Your Honor. And you can download the R&amp;D for it to the DOST. If you don't have a budget for risk capital, then you cannot derive any benefits whatsoever. It's just like people in the mining industry. If you don't spend for the exploration, which is risky, I mean, how can you value something properly?

asr-001616
02:16:38.780 --> 02:16:56.020
Rep. Johanne Monich G. Bautista: Thank you, Madam Chair and Mr. Secretary. Just wanted to thank the Secretary and commit to look into the proposed suggestions of Mr. Secretary to amend the law and ensure its implementation. Thank you, Madam Chair.

asr-001625
02:16:57.300 --> 02:17:37.480
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Thank you, Congressman Johanne Bautista. Uh, at this point, I would like to acknowledge the additional, uh, House members, um, who are present today. Uh, Congressman Junard "Ahong" Chan, uh, Vice Chair Joboy Aquino, uh, Representative J.J. Romualdo, Representative Ferdinand Beltran, Representative Elijah San Fernando, Assistant Majority Leader De Carlo "Oyo" Uy, and Representative Samier Tan. Next to interpolate, from the minority, Congressman Egay Erice.

asr-001645
02:17:39.820 --> 02:20:25.360
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Good morning, Secretary Teodoro and the rest of the DND family. My father was my late father was a former member of the Philippine Air Force. A non-commissioned officer before he worked with Air America in Vietnam. So we have a long relations with the U.S. At the same time, we have also a very long relations with China. With the U.S. militarily, with China, economically. So foreign policy really is as I see it now, it's really, you know, I think there's a divergence between the statements of President Marcos and Secretary Teodoro. Well, it might be a strategic way of doing things, but there's also dangers. So let me just let me just for example, President Marcos says that we need a reset in terms of relations with China. Secretary Teodoro says broader defense engagement with China is impossible because China lacks good faith. Marcos says China remains an important investment and economic partner. Secretary Teodoro says China uses coercion, blackmail, and foreign influence. President Marcos discusses joint oil exploration. Meanwhile, the Philippine defense system becomes increasingly interoperable with the United States, especially with the EDCA sites. So, there might be a decline on the trust on both countries, the U.S. and China. Ayoko na pong ayoko pong pangunahan yung strategy as a strategy. As I very well know that the President is the chief architect of foreign policy. However, there are public concerns. At ito po yung gusto ko sana itanong. First question, po, Secretary. What exactly triggers the Mutual Defense Treaty?

asr-001725
02:20:26.700 --> 02:21:16.600
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: The triggering of Article 5 of the Mutual Defense Treaty, is a call of the Philippine government or the U.S. government if an attack is made on either country, public vessel, and the like. So, the trigger really is a call of an executive or the triggering party. Here, it will be the President of the Philippines based on an attack, or any public vessel, if he feels that Article 5, which is the active portion of the Mutual Defense Treaty, comes into play.

asr-001747
02:21:18.680 --> 02:21:33.040
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: What happens if China and the U.S. engage in the Taiwan War? What are the possibilities of the Philippines participating in this?

asr-001753
02:21:33.320 --> 02:21:40.340
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: The President has made clear, Your Honor, that the Philippines is constitutionally prohibited from engaging in foreign—

asr-001757
02:21:40.740 --> 02:21:40.980
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Pardon?

asr-001758
02:21:40.980 --> 02:21:49.240
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: The President has made clear that the Philippines is prohibited from engaging in any offensive activity, so it's purely defensive.

asr-001762
02:21:49.900 --> 02:22:00.080
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: But the U.S. might use the EDCA sites, several EDCA sites in the Philippines to launch their attacks.

asr-001767
02:22:00.460 --> 02:22:03.660
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: That's a speculative thing, might, but it has not.

asr-001770
02:22:03.740 --> 02:22:04.900
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: It's a reality.

asr-001771
02:22:06.600 --> 02:22:10.220
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Under the President's guidance, it cannot.

asr-001773
02:22:12.800 --> 02:22:16.720
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: So it remains to be speculative as far as you are concerned?

asr-001775
02:22:16.720 --> 02:22:25.500
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Oh, sure, Your Honor. It's speculative, but insofar as the President's guidance is concerned, it cannot be used for any external factor.

asr-001779
02:22:25.500 --> 02:22:29.640
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Can they use the Philippine territory during the Taiwan conflict?

asr-001781
02:22:29.640 --> 02:22:37.580
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: The EDCA sites? It can only be used if, Your Honor, the Philippines is under attack or threat.

asr-001786
02:22:37.580 --> 02:22:40.220
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: So this is very clear in the...

asr-001788
02:22:40.220 --> 02:22:40.880
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Oh, yes, Your Honor.

asr-001789
02:22:41.220 --> 02:22:41.580
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: ...in the treaty.

asr-001790
02:22:41.580 --> 02:22:49.440
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: It is clear. And under the agreement on enhanced defense cooperation, it cannot violate any Philippine law or the Constitution.

asr-001796
02:22:49.440 --> 02:22:54.800
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Could U.S. offensive missiles be permanently positioned here?

asr-001798
02:22:54.800 --> 02:23:01.200
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: If they're with the Philippines, Your Honor, then we will welcome them if they're under the Philippine armed forces.

asr-001803
02:23:01.990 --> 02:23:03.500
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Pardon, Mr. Secretary, I can barely hear you.

asr-001805
02:23:03.500 --> 02:23:07.920
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: The Philippine arsenal, Your Honor.

asr-001808
02:23:10.620 --> 02:23:13.080
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: so they can launch a missile attack to China?

asr-001810
02:23:13.080 --> 02:23:19.200
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: The Philippines will launch, Your Honor, if ever. If they become part of the armed forces of the Philippines, we will welcome them.

asr-001816
02:23:20.180 --> 02:23:29.080
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: So your answer is they cannot use offensive missiles from Philippine territory? From Philippine territory.

asr-001821
02:23:29.080 --> 02:23:35.120
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: No, Your Honor, for offensive purposes, unless Article 5 is activated. It's to defend the Philippines.

asr-001825
02:23:38.240 --> 02:23:43.720
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: And what is our long-term West Philippine Sea Objective?

asr-001828
02:23:43.720 --> 02:23:56.760
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: The long-term West Philippine Sea Objective, Your Honor, it remains the same under the Constitution. It's to explore and exploit for the Filipinos each and every item in there that we can.

asr-001839
02:23:56.760 --> 02:24:06.200
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: So, how would you relate this to the pronouncement of the President that we can have joint oil exploration to China?

asr-001846
02:24:06.200 --> 02:24:10.300
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Well, that's subject to Philippine law, Your Honor, and the Constitution.

asr-001850
02:24:13.500 --> 02:24:34.060
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: And it, when it comes to, because, you know, there are millions of Filipino-Chinese here in the Philippines. In fact, Secretary Teodoro, you are a Cojuangco with Chinese roots. Am I right?

asr-001862
02:24:34.400 --> 02:24:36.520
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Oh, yeah. Seven generations ago.

asr-001864
02:24:36.620 --> 02:25:14.399
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Yes, yes. And I talked to the Filipino Chinese Chamber of Commerce here. There are about 200,000 or more Chinese who illegally enter the Philippines with fake documents provided by agencies of our government. And they are not now so worried with what's happening even when, for example, when you conducted a raid involving [unclear]—

asr-001885
02:25:14.399 --> 02:25:15.439
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Oh, yes, Your Honor.

asr-001886
02:25:15.439 --> 02:25:16.790
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: —in Cagayan de Oro.

asr-001890
02:25:16.800 --> 02:25:19.175
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: And where is it located, Your Honor?

asr-001892
02:25:19.175 --> 02:25:21.706
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: The Philippine Veterans Industrial Estate.

asr-001894
02:25:21.740 --> 02:25:25.120
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Yes. That is a supervised agency under DND.

asr-001897
02:25:25.220 --> 02:25:32.460
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: So, there is no business for anyone doing illegal activities in there. Doing what?

asr-001904
02:25:32.460 --> 02:25:42.660
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Illegal activities, Your Honor. Which is why there is a closure order by DENR and a revocation of its ECC.

asr-001913
02:25:42.660 --> 02:25:47.320
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: And can the civilian agencies do that—

asr-001916
02:25:47.320 --> 02:25:47.940
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: or—

asr-001917
02:25:47.940 --> 02:25:50.120
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Of course, Your Honor. Yes.

asr-001920
02:25:50.120 --> 02:25:53.020
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: And why would the DND be involved?

asr-001922
02:25:53.020 --> 02:26:00.540
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Because PHIVIDEC, Your Honor, is a supervised agency under DND.

asr-001928
02:26:02.460 --> 02:26:04.220
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: A supervised agency?

asr-001930
02:26:04.220 --> 02:26:09.100
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: It is a GOCC supervised by DND.

asr-001934
02:26:09.100 --> 02:26:12.000
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: So the GOCC is under DND?

asr-001937
02:26:12.000 --> 02:26:14.220
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: It is attached to DND.

asr-001939
02:26:14.720 --> 02:26:15.820
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Attached to DND.

asr-001941
02:26:15.820 --> 02:26:16.640
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Yes, Your Honor.

asr-001943
02:26:16.640 --> 02:26:29.180
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: And the DND under 6975 still has a mandate for internal and national security. Okay. Can you specifically state what's the illegal activity?

asr-001952
02:26:29.180 --> 02:26:48.900
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Producing substandard steel, Your Honor, which did not pass regulations. Environmental damage, Your Honor. Having radioactively tainted scrap metals in there. And danger to the workers.

asr-001969
02:26:48.900 --> 02:26:54.300
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: But no espionage or military issues?

asr-001973
02:26:55.480 --> 02:27:03.380
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: The military issue there, Your Honor, was it was in PHIVIDEC. Jurisdictionally.

asr-001979
02:27:03.380 --> 02:27:14.460
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Oh, okay. Under the DND. There's no allegation that's being used by the Chinese government for any espionage activity or something?

asr-001991
02:27:14.460 --> 02:27:47.260
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: There is no evidence, Your Honor, but I will leave that to the law enforcement authorities, the NBI, who actually got a warrant, search warrant from a court before entering into the area. Yes. And these are law enforcement operations. Before doing so, a search warrant valid was taken, Your Honor. It was not a unilateral entry without judicial authority.

asr-002024
02:27:47.260 --> 02:28:14.100
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: And there's also the case of Joseph Sy, a mining owner here in the Philippines who has fake documents and he was being incarcerated for at least for almost a year. And there's also an allegation that he's a Chinese government spy. Do you have any information on that?

asr-002048
02:28:14.100 --> 02:28:26.640
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: The allegation I know of Joseph Sy, Your Honor, is fake citizenship. No espionage issue. As far as I know, there was none. It's a BI issue, Your Honor.

asr-002061
02:28:26.640 --> 02:28:30.780
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: It's a BI issue. Yeah. Thank you, Secretary. Thank you.

