DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: I'll try to find out, Your Honor.

asr-003249-split-2
03:44:34.364 --> 03:44:36.229
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Thank you very much,

asr-003250
03:44:36.239 --> 03:44:37.269
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Madam Chair.

asr-003251
03:44:37.279 --> 03:44:39.110
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: My next question po, it would be in relation to

asr-003252
03:44:39.120 --> 03:44:40.950
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: also questions asked

asr-003253
03:44:40.960 --> 03:44:42.527
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: last time.

asr-003254
03:44:42.536 --> 03:44:44.540
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Nagkaroon po tayo ng

asr-003255
03:44:44.540 --> 03:44:46.545
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: pag-share or even ng unity na

asr-003256
03:44:46.545 --> 03:44:48.198
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: i-reconsider

asr-003257
03:44:48.198 --> 03:44:55.153
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: reconsider yung pag-procure ng arms through Elbit Systems. Meron po bang bagong

asr-003258
03:44:55.153 --> 03:44:59.964
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: contracts or bagong mga arms procured through Elbit Systems, Madam Chair?

asr-003259
03:45:00.786 --> 03:45:06.177
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: We just need, Your Honor, to replenish the missile systems that were used in

asr-003260
03:45:06.177 --> 03:45:13.674
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: training, but there are no additional or new contracts with LBIT systems.

asr-003261
03:45:13.674 --> 03:45:19.546
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Okay. Related also to questions kanina po ng Representative San Fernando,

asr-003262
03:45:19.727 --> 03:45:24.357
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: meron po bang steps that the DND has taken to reduce the dependence of the

asr-003263
03:45:24.357 --> 03:45:29.207
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Philippines on the importation of arms? Meron po bang local arms manufacturing

asr-003264
03:45:29.207 --> 03:45:30.611
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: na in-explore na mangyayari?

asr-003265
03:45:31.120 --> 03:45:38.468
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Your Honor, it's not the capability we need. And the capabilities of local arms

asr-003266
03:45:38.468 --> 03:45:43.479
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: manufacturers are for small arms, which is not...

asr-003267
03:45:43.739 --> 03:45:50.815
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: not where the DND wants to go, actually. Even the government arsenal.

asr-003268
03:45:52.000 --> 03:46:00.015
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: We need more domain awareness, we need more internal hardening systems, and we

asr-003269
03:46:00.015 --> 03:46:09.656
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: need more deterrent systems. I hope that local industry will come to such a

asr-003270
03:46:09.656 --> 03:46:14.045
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: stage, Your Honor, but at this stage, we cannot afford to be on the...

asr-003271
03:46:15.087 --> 03:46:23.305
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: backside of the learning curve, given the fact that the evolution of

asr-003272
03:46:23.305 --> 03:46:34.911
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: technology is really, really quick and really fast. And to handhold industries,

asr-003273
03:46:34.911 --> 03:46:44.692
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: which, on an industry basis, Your Honor, if we can scale the production, which industry must,

asr-003274
03:46:44.800 --> 03:46:50.545
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: have the capacity for, in terms of value propositions, then it's fine.

asr-003275
03:46:50.545 --> 03:47:01.869
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: But it must be forward-looking, and they must not cater to what would normally be a police item,

asr-003276
03:47:02.270 --> 03:47:10.869
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: or something that we need to move, not beyond, but in addition to.

asr-003277
03:47:11.871 --> 03:47:14.397
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Okay. So, Madam Chair, tama.

asr-003278
03:47:15.218 --> 03:47:21.131
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: na yung mga acquisition of arms na beyond yung small arms ay nandiyan naman sa budget,

asr-003279
03:47:21.552 --> 03:47:23.677
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: including po ba drones, et cetera?

asr-003280
03:47:25.120 --> 03:47:32.229
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Drones per se, Your Honor, are, you know, of course, part of the toolkit of any country right now,

asr-003281
03:47:32.239 --> 03:47:39.429
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: but the production of drones is quite easy. It's the technology you put in depending on what you want to use them for.

asr-003282
03:47:39.439 --> 03:47:43.017
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: So, meron po bang local production of drones, or kasama rin siya sa importation, Madam Chair?

asr-003284
03:47:43.027 --> 03:47:52.950
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: I'm sure there are, Your Honor. This is easily done. But it's what you carry them, what you put into them, actually, which is important, and which changes.

asr-003285
03:47:52.960 --> 03:48:01.110
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Because of the advent of AI, it changes every three days, sometimes.

asr-003286
03:48:01.359 --> 03:48:06.206
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: May operational guidelines po ba sa usage of drones ng military, Madam Chair, right now?

asr-003287
03:48:06.206 --> 03:48:08.077
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Your Honor, it's on the evolution stage.

asr-003288
03:48:08.813 --> 03:48:14.646
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: So, right now, wala pong written guidelines? Because meron po ang commercial, so sa military right now, wala pa?

asr-003289
03:48:15.004 --> 03:48:17.751
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Wala pa po. We are still evolving the technology.

asr-003290
03:48:18.129 --> 03:48:25.097
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: And actually, in order to use drones, we have to develop our backbone systems in order to use this responsibly.

asr-003291
03:48:26.132 --> 03:48:32.581
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Ako, I'd like to flag that, Madam Chair. As you said po, as the Secretary said, kailangan po ng responsible use.

asr-003292
03:48:32.721 --> 03:48:41.599
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: And I think it starts at guidelines. Kung paano po siyempre gamitin, lalo na it's possible na pwedeng ma-abuse.

asr-003293
03:48:41.599 --> 03:48:44.843
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: So, kailan po ba maasahan, if ever, na magka-guidelines?

asr-003294
03:48:44.863 --> 03:48:51.094
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Right now po, there are no offensive uses for drones, insofar as we're concerned.

asr-003295
03:48:51.359 --> 03:49:01.385
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Uh, they are for surveillance, but naturally, we will conform with guidelines for the external defense use of drones,

asr-003296
03:49:02.160 --> 03:49:04.908
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: if it is for purposes other than surveillance.

asr-003297
03:49:05.744 --> 03:49:13.886
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Kung meron pong mga updates tungkol po sa pagkaroon ng guidelines on its operations,

asr-003298
03:49:14.244 --> 03:49:16.295
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: magkaroon po sana ng copy na maipasa.

asr-003299
03:49:16.314 --> 03:49:19.659
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: So, through this committee, para po ma-insure yung responsible use sa kanya.

asr-003300
03:49:20.216 --> 03:49:27.721
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Much as they are disclosable, Your Honor, I don't think it's anything wrong,

asr-003301
03:49:27.840 --> 03:49:36.241
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: just as long as the nuts and bolts and the granularity that may compromise our systems are not compromised.

asr-003302
03:49:37.359 --> 03:49:41.189
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: For now, no more questions given the limitations and time.

asr-003303
03:49:41.199 --> 03:49:45.830
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Madam Chair, I would like to sign up for the second round. Thank you.

asr-003304
03:49:45.840 --> 03:49:48.955
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Yes, thank you, Cong. Renee Co.

asr-003305
03:49:48.965 --> 03:49:53.510
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Next to interpolate from the majority, Vice Chair Rufus Rodriguez.

asr-003306
03:49:53.920 --> 03:49:56.960
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Thank you, Madam Chair, Chair Bella Suansing.

asr-003307
03:49:58.640 --> 03:50:02.160
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: A pleasant good afternoon to the Department of National Defense Officialdom

asr-003308
03:50:04.000 --> 03:50:06.080
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: and also the Armed Forces of the Philippines.

asr-003309
03:50:08.720 --> 03:50:10.720
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: First, let me congratulate and thank Secretary Teodoro

asr-003310
03:50:15.120 --> 03:50:15.680
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: for being a patriot.

asr-003311
03:50:18.160 --> 03:50:19.760
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: For fighting for the West Philippine Sea

asr-003312
03:50:21.359 --> 03:50:26.399
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: and standing up against China, the bully of our region.

asr-003313
03:50:27.600 --> 03:50:31.040
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: So, you are, you have been able, since the time you were Secretary,

asr-003314
03:50:32.800 --> 03:50:34.319
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: you were able to protect Philippine interests

asr-003315
03:50:36.399 --> 03:50:40.399
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: as there should be no other interest paramount to our sovereignty.

asr-003316
03:50:41.920 --> 03:50:44.560
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: It is Article 1 of the Philippine Constitution.

asr-003317
03:50:46.319 --> 03:50:52.960
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: It also goes without saying that he is our pride of the U.P. College of Law.

asr-003318
03:50:56.640 --> 03:51:00.399
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Having number one in the bar examinations, I was only number 17.

asr-003319
03:51:01.840 --> 03:51:07.600
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: So, I have to bring this list by the Taliba who were in the top 20

asr-003320
03:51:07.920 --> 03:51:10.960
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: because nobody believes if you are number 11 to 20.

asr-003321
03:51:12.080 --> 03:51:14.479
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: But no doubt that Secretary Gilbert,

asr-003322
03:51:16.720 --> 03:51:18.000
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Secretary Teodoro, number one in the bar.

asr-003323
03:51:18.960 --> 03:51:20.239
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: So, I have a question.

asr-003324
03:51:20.640 --> 03:51:29.520
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Number one is, what is the budget of the DND for the Lumbia 15th Strike Wing?

asr-003325
03:51:32.408 --> 03:51:33.510
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: If that is right, yeah.

asr-003326
03:51:33.920 --> 03:51:40.399
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: What is now the budget for 2027 to further develop our Lumbia EDCA site?

asr-003327
03:51:46.800 --> 03:51:50.160
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Your Honor, I beg a few seconds to retrieve the data.

asr-003328
03:51:52.800 --> 03:52:08.720
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: In the facilities, for this year, Your Honor, it's 115 million.

asr-003329
03:52:10.647 --> 03:52:11.913
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: But again, for this year, 2026?

asr-003330
03:52:14.157 --> 03:52:15.457
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Yeah, yeah, 115.

asr-003331
03:52:16.324 --> 03:52:17.030
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Million?

asr-003332
03:52:17.040 --> 03:52:18.000
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Yes, Your Honor, that's the remaining.

asr-003333
03:52:18.960 --> 03:52:19.840
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: And for next year?

asr-003334
03:52:20.654 --> 03:52:22.814
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: That's the remaining, Your Honor.

asr-003335
03:52:23.067 --> 03:52:23.843
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Completed?

asr-003336
03:52:23.978 --> 03:52:24.502
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Yes, Your Honor.

asr-003337
03:52:24.960 --> 03:52:25.840
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Yes, thank you. 115 million.

asr-003338
03:52:26.160 --> 03:52:26.880
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: So, there's already a budget.

asr-003339
03:52:28.000 --> 03:52:29.760
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Save enhancements that may be done.

asr-003340
03:52:31.150 --> 03:52:31.750
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Thank you.

asr-003341
03:52:31.840 --> 03:52:35.279
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: And what is now also the counterpart of the United States Government? Being an EDCA site?

asr-003343
03:52:39.199 --> 03:52:39.760
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Not yet, Your Honor.

asr-003344
03:52:41.359 --> 03:52:43.760
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: I thought as EDCA site,

asr-003345
03:52:44.560 --> 03:52:52.160
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: there will already be infusion of American dollars to further develop that Lumbia airport.

asr-003346
03:52:53.600 --> 03:52:58.560
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Your Honor, the development of, even for us, for the 15th Strike Wing,

asr-003347
03:53:00.125 --> 03:53:01.750
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: and to have a maintenance base.

asr-003348
03:53:01.760 --> 03:53:03.199
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Maintenance base. They're hampered by right-of-way issues.

asr-003350
03:53:06.800 --> 03:53:07.680
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: What is the problem?

asr-003351
03:53:09.840 --> 03:53:10.479
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Informal settlers,

asr-003352
03:53:11.000 --> 03:53:13.000
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Your Honor, that has hampered us.

asr-003354
03:53:14.960 --> 03:53:16.479
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: And it's only now that we have

asr-003356
03:53:18.720 --> 03:53:20.479
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: taken the appropriate

asr-003357
03:53:21.359 --> 03:53:22.160
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: legal proceedings and

asr-003358
03:53:23.199 --> 03:53:24.319
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: working towards looking for

asr-003359
03:53:24.560 --> 03:53:25.120
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: adequate relocation for us

asr-003361
03:53:28.800 --> 03:53:29.760
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: to fully utilize,

asr-003362
03:53:30.560 --> 03:53:32.500
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: not only for the 15th Strike Wing,

asr-003364
03:53:35.600 --> 03:53:36.560
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: but it shall serve as the

asr-003366
03:53:38.720 --> 03:53:42.300
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Northern Mindanao Operations Center for the OCD.

asr-003370
03:53:48.800 --> 03:53:50.399
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: There are still illegal settlers

asr-003371
03:53:51.120 --> 03:53:52.640
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: and the access road to the highway,

asr-003372
03:53:53.040 --> 03:53:54.479
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Your Honor, to the highway.

asr-003373
03:53:55.711 --> 03:53:56.950
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Thank you, Secretary

asr-003374
03:53:57.359 --> 03:53:58.479
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Gibo. Now, in the

asr-003375
03:53:58.800 --> 03:54:00.399
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: master plan, what is the contribution of

asr-003377
03:54:02.399 --> 03:54:02.960
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: the United States Government

asr-003378
03:54:03.760 --> 03:54:05.359
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: to the Lumbia Airport?

asr-003380
03:54:07.591 --> 03:54:10.021
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: They are still scoping, Your Honor,

asr-003381
03:54:10.510 --> 03:54:12.950
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: what they can do with the area, particularly knowing that

asr-003383
03:54:14.342 --> 03:54:15.750
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: again, Cagayan de Oro is

asr-003384
03:54:15.760 --> 03:54:16.560
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: vulnerable to mudslides.

asr-003385
03:54:17.600 --> 03:54:19.199
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: And since it will be also a

asr-003387
03:54:22.720 --> 03:54:23.439
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: coordination center

asr-003388
03:54:23.760 --> 03:54:25.199
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: for Northern Mindanao for HADR,

asr-003389
03:54:26.640 --> 03:54:27.600
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: they're scoping in those

asr-003390
03:54:27.840 --> 03:54:28.640
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: lines, Your Honor.

asr-003391
03:54:34.730 --> 03:54:35.591
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: They're scoping,

asr-003392
03:54:35.840 --> 03:54:39.600
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: The scoping is for a multipurpose warehouse, and for us,

asr-003393
03:54:39.840 --> 03:54:41.199
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Your Honor, it's air traffic control enhancement.

asr-003394
03:54:43.439 --> 03:54:44.800
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: So, in the plan, what is the structures

asr-003395
03:54:46.080 --> 03:54:46.960
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: to be built by the U.S.

asr-003396
03:54:48.800 --> 03:54:49.420
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Government?

asr-003397
03:54:50.160 --> 03:54:51.040
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: So far, there's nothing agreed,

asr-003398
03:54:51.520 --> 03:54:53.040
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Your Honor. They're scoping for a warehouse.

asr-003399
03:54:56.731 --> 03:54:56.870
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Warehouse.

asr-003400
03:54:56.880 --> 03:54:59.840
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: There will be social costs when the Americans would go there.

asr-003401
03:55:00.399 --> 03:55:03.920
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: What are the plans of our Armed Forces of the Philippines and the DND?

asr-003402
03:55:06.880 --> 03:55:07.520
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: On social costs,

asr-003403
03:55:08.080 --> 03:55:09.199
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Your Honor, that's why the right-of-way issues

asr-003404
03:55:09.760 --> 03:55:10.399
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: will be the first.

asr-003405
03:55:12.319 --> 03:55:14.399
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: And the

asr-003406
03:55:14.640 --> 03:55:15.279
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: relocation issues

asr-003407
03:55:15.760 --> 03:55:17.680
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: will be the most important thing, which we are

asr-003408
03:55:18.399 --> 03:55:19.439
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: addressing, because we need to address

asr-003409
03:55:19.920 --> 03:55:21.040
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: it in order to provide base security.

asr-003412
03:55:24.592 --> 03:55:27.830
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Referring to, you know, when there are Americans,

asr-003413
03:55:27.840 --> 03:55:29.040
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: you know, there will be prostitution.

asr-003414
03:55:34.000 --> 03:55:34.640
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Your Honor, there will be...

asr-003415
03:55:35.120 --> 03:55:36.560
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Any plans for that to protect?

asr-003417
03:55:36.995 --> 03:55:39.037
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: our women in Cagayan de Oro.

asr-003418
03:55:39.680 --> 03:55:44.239
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: No, they will be guided by SOFA, Your Honor, if ever they are there, present, you know, and...

asr-003419
03:55:45.199 --> 03:55:48.000
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: The SOFA will provide for how do we protect our women of Cagayan de Oro.

asr-003420
03:55:48.800 --> 03:55:50.800
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Yes, Your Honor, in the same way as they should be protected

asr-003421
03:55:52.399 --> 03:55:57.199
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: from our own exploitation by our own men, too.

asr-003422
03:55:58.207 --> 03:55:59.600
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Thank you, Secretary.

asr-003423
03:55:59.680 --> 03:56:06.640
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Next question is, how is now the proposed naval base in our neighboring town of Tagoloan?

asr-003425
03:56:08.960 --> 03:56:10.239
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: That will be the dockyard, Your Honor.

asr-003426
03:56:11.040 --> 03:56:11.920
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: It's still awaiting finalization of the titling.

asr-003428
03:56:15.976 --> 03:56:16.600
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: The titling?

asr-003429
03:56:16.600 --> 03:56:17.039
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Yes, Your Honor.

asr-003430
03:56:17.439 --> 03:56:19.199
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Is that in the PHIVIDEC area, Honorable Secretary?

asr-003431
03:56:20.720 --> 03:56:21.680
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: It is the southern...

asr-003432
03:56:24.319 --> 03:56:26.960
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: It is in the southern portion of the PHIVIDEC area, Your Honor.

asr-003433
03:56:28.399 --> 03:56:30.399
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: How much will that entail in cost

asr-003434
03:56:31.040 --> 03:56:33.279
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: once the titling is already done?

asr-003435
03:56:36.867 --> 03:56:39.439
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: For a complete dry dock.

asr-003436
03:56:40.239 --> 03:56:45.279
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Your Honor, that will be able to support our fleet, growing fleet.

asr-003437
03:56:45.600 --> 03:56:47.040
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: That's about 40 billion pesos.

asr-003438
03:56:49.473 --> 03:56:50.630
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: How much, Secretary?

asr-003439
03:56:50.640 --> 03:56:52.640
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Forty. Forty billion, Your Honor.

asr-003440
03:56:53.120 --> 03:56:54.399
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Ah, the cost of the dry dock is 40 billion?

asr-003441
03:56:55.227 --> 03:56:55.328
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Indeed.

asr-003442
03:56:56.020 --> 03:56:57.100
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: The whole thing, Your Honor.

asr-003443
03:56:57.100 --> 03:56:57.607
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Whole thing?

asr-003444
03:56:57.607 --> 03:56:58.568
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Together with equipment.

asr-003445
03:56:59.680 --> 03:57:04.319
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Indeed, that will bring forth substantial economic activity for Cagayan de Oro.

asr-003446
03:57:04.330 --> 03:57:08.913
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Thank you very much for that, Secretary.

asr-003448
03:57:08.913 --> 03:57:09.976
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: From there.

asr-003449
03:57:09.976 --> 03:57:10.465
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Yes.

asr-003450
03:57:10.560 --> 03:57:15.199
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: It's strategic because it can be a dry dock

asr-003451
03:57:15.520 --> 03:57:17.359
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: because it's relatively free from typhoons.

asr-003452
03:57:19.760 --> 03:57:25.600
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: And it can accommodate even the largest vessel, which is an LPD.

asr-003453
03:57:26.800 --> 03:57:30.960
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: But because the Subic Naval Base right now is...

asr-003454
03:57:31.840 --> 03:57:33.439
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: We cannot use it as a dry dock.

asr-003455
03:57:36.399 --> 03:57:38.160
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: It's an operating naval base.

asr-003456
03:57:38.800 --> 03:57:39.439
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: This one will be adopted.

asr-003457
03:57:39.600 --> 03:57:43.920
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: It is a real dry dock where we can adequately maintain and supervise all our vessels.

asr-003458
03:57:45.040 --> 03:57:54.560
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: So, thank you for thinking of relocating it in Misamis Oriental, in Tagoloan, which is beside the city of Cagayan de Oro, the city of golden friendship.

asr-003459
03:57:56.640 --> 03:57:57.520
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: So, we thank you for that, Secretary.

asr-003460
03:57:58.080 --> 03:58:00.000
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: And when will the title be?

asr-003461
03:58:00.319 --> 03:58:01.750
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: What is the timetable?

asr-003462
03:58:01.760 --> 03:58:05.040
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Of course, you have lawyers and the title would be finished about when.

asr-003463
03:58:05.600 --> 03:58:08.160
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: And when will the start of the construction be?

asr-003464
03:58:08.399 --> 03:58:09.040
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: We're awaiting that.

asr-003465
03:58:09.612 --> 03:58:12.262
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: For Cagayan de Oro and Misamis Oriental.

asr-003466
03:58:12.262 --> 03:58:13.510
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Your Honor, I await too.

asr-003467
03:58:13.520 --> 03:58:16.319
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: And we're trying our level best to get the titling done.

asr-003468
03:58:16.960 --> 03:58:21.920
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Because we need to leave, vacate Sangley as soon as possible

asr-003469
03:58:22.399 --> 03:58:24.960
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: because it is extremely shallow, extremely small.

asr-003470
03:58:26.160 --> 03:58:30.239
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: And it's getting to be unmaneuverable for our naval platforms.

asr-003471
03:58:32.208 --> 03:58:32.790
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Thank you.

asr-003472
03:58:32.800 --> 03:58:38.319
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: That is good news to Mindanao, specifically Northern Mindanao and entire Mindanao, and Cagayan de Oro and Misamis Oriental.

asr-003473
03:58:40.479 --> 03:58:48.960
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: My other question, Mr. Secretary, is before there were talks about the transfer of the 4th military area which we oppose,

asr-003474
03:58:50.080 --> 03:58:57.359
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: are there still plans to transfer the 4th Infantry Division in Cagayan de Oro, Patag, to another place?

asr-003475
03:58:58.479 --> 03:59:00.000
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: That is not a specific guidance, Your Honor.

asr-003476
03:59:00.399 --> 03:59:03.120
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Our specific guidance is for the Army to relocate.

asr-003477
03:59:05.600 --> 03:59:09.279
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: To scope their areas where they need to have the homes

asr-003478
03:59:09.760 --> 03:59:12.160
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Of their divisions and brigades.

asr-003479
03:59:14.399 --> 03:59:22.960
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: With respect to having a division headquarters or a brigade headquarters as a connectivity node,

asr-003480
03:59:24.800 --> 03:59:29.279
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: as a logistical supply point, as a motor pool,

asr-003481
03:59:32.080 --> 03:59:36.720
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: and for divisions to contain medical facilities adequately to support.

asr-003482
03:59:38.000 --> 03:59:39.279
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: And this must be able to...

asr-003483
03:59:39.760 --> 03:59:43.520
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Provide connectivity to strategic bases of other services.

asr-003484
03:59:45.279 --> 03:59:46.880
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: If not, then the strategic bases...

asr-003485
03:59:47.520 --> 03:59:56.880
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: bases cannot be resupplied adequately, so it is a whole exercise in logistics, Your Honor, and I know

asr-003486
03:59:57.040 --> 04:00:06.640
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: there are certain legacy areas which first have developed massive roots already and we will keep

asr-003487
04:00:06.800 --> 04:00:14.479
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: this into consideration nonetheless the exercise really is in logistics your honor because we have

asr-003488
04:00:14.560 --> 04:00:20.319
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: a very very big difficulty particularly in humanitarian assistance and disaster response

asr-003489
04:00:20.800 --> 04:00:30.319
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: and resupplying our own troops it's quite difficult so we need to have the logistics

asr-003490
04:00:30.960 --> 04:00:40.560
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: capabilities in order for the armed forces to pursue its uh external defense role thank you

asr-003491
04:00:40.800 --> 04:00:44.160
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Secretary, you know, Patag

asr-003492
04:00:44.880 --> 04:00:52.239
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: for the division is really very, very strategically located. Of course, Cagayan de Oro is the gateway to

asr-003493
04:00:54.880 --> 04:00:59.760
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Mindanao. If we talk about Davao, you go around the Zamboanga Peninsula, and so in

asr-003494
04:01:00.239 --> 04:01:06.160
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: terms of logistics that's the best side and I believe that there is still uh area that will

asr-003495
04:01:06.399 --> 04:01:12.800
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: be used for that. So we ask you on behalf of the city of Cagayan de Oro to consider that as the

asr-003496
04:01:13.608 --> 04:01:14.252
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: continuing

asr-003497
04:01:14.960 --> 04:01:21.600
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: area for the Armed Forces because it is very strategically located. From Cagayan de Oro, you

asr-003498
04:01:21.680 --> 04:01:29.760
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: go to Bukidnon, and then you go to Butuan. So please consider that, Mr. Secretary, because we would wish

asr-003499
04:01:29.920 --> 04:01:37.600
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: that to remain in the city of Cagayan de Oro. On the three domains—

asr-003500
04:01:38.160 --> 04:01:43.760
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Your Honor, and the fourth domain, the cyber domain and the IT domain, that is indeed a valuable

asr-003501
04:01:46.160 --> 04:01:50.399
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: position, and as a matter of fact we are adding on the naval domain with the dockyard that is

asr-003502
04:01:51.680 --> 04:01:59.040
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: proposed, and Lumbia as the home of the 15th Strike Wing where they will train and they will

asr-003503
04:01:59.199 --> 04:02:10.000
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: maintain, and it will also be the home of the Northern Mindanao Operations Center

asr-003504
04:02:10.319 --> 04:02:16.560
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: of the OCD.

asr-003505
04:02:18.800 --> 04:02:25.680
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: So, Your Honor, rest assured that that is an area of prime consideration for us.

asr-003506
04:02:26.960 --> 04:02:38.229
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Thank you, Secretary Gibo. It now looks that, uh, the Secretary is looking at Cagayan de Oro and Misamis Oriental. We have the 15th Strike Wing

asr-003508
04:02:38.239 --> 04:02:42.880
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: in Lumbia, and then we have the dockyard, 40 billion, in

asr-003510
04:02:43.680 --> 04:02:56.000
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: in the municipality, and then our Army is there in Patag to be enlarged to become a logistical

asr-003511
04:02:56.560 --> 04:03:02.640
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: center because Cagayan de Oro is the center of Northern Mindanao and gateway to entire Mindanao.

asr-003512
04:03:03.600 --> 04:03:10.160
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: So, with that we thank the Secretary for the Lumbia airport, we thank the Secretary for the dockyard,

asr-003513
04:03:11.359 --> 04:03:17.600
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: and we thank the Secretary for enlarging the 4th Infantry Division. Thank you, Mr. Secretary.

asr-003514
04:03:18.960 --> 04:03:23.840
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Again, we thank you for your service to this nation, which is unequaled in recent history.

asr-003515
04:03:24.479 --> 04:03:25.377
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Thank you very much.

asr-003515-b
04:03:26.255 --> 04:03:27.115
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Thank you, Your Honor.

asr-003516
04:03:29.022 --> 04:03:38.000
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Thank you, Vice Chair Rufus Rodriguez. Given that there are no other minority members who are listed for the first round, we will proceed

asr-003517
04:03:38.319 --> 04:03:40.239
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: with the majority members.

asr-003518
04:03:41.760 --> 04:03:46.741
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: So, from the majority, the next to interpolate, Rep. Marlo Bancoro.

asr-003519
04:03:51.027 --> 04:04:02.198
Rep. Marlo C. Bancoro: Thank you, Madam Chair. Good afternoon, my dear colleagues. Good afternoon, Secretary Gibo and the DND family. Mine is just a

asr-003520
04:04:03.160 --> 04:04:05.438
Rep. Marlo C. Bancoro: parochial concern, Secretary.

asr-003521
04:04:06.687 --> 04:04:08.459
Rep. Marlo C. Bancoro: My proposal is a

asr-003522
04:04:09.455 --> 04:04:17.943
Rep. Marlo C. Bancoro: joint camp with the PNP, Army, and Coast Guard,

asr-003523
04:04:18.803 --> 04:04:20.187
Rep. Marlo C. Bancoro: and the

asr-003524
04:04:20.660 --> 04:04:24.102
Rep. Marlo C. Bancoro: previous Chief of Staff [unclear].

asr-003525
04:04:24.743 --> 04:04:33.367
Rep. Marlo C. Bancoro: It will be implemented by the local government unit of [unclear], where the island is situated

asr-003526
04:04:34.126 --> 04:04:42.074
Rep. Marlo C. Bancoro: and on which the camp is going to be constructed. So my concern

asr-003527
04:04:43.087 --> 04:04:54.000
Rep. Marlo C. Bancoro: is the request of the regional director [unclear] the PNP [unclear]

asr-003528
04:04:54.038 --> 04:05:00.282
Rep. Marlo C. Bancoro: the council of the PNP [unclear], the Coast Guard, and the commission for the Coast Guard [unclear]

asr-003529
04:05:00.282 --> 04:05:06.745
Rep. Marlo C. Bancoro: of the MOA for the downloading of the funds, and the PNP supposedly by August 27 also. Unfortunately, it's

asr-003530
04:05:06.982 --> 04:05:11.825
Rep. Marlo C. Bancoro: scheduled [unclear] for the budget hearing. [Unclear] PNP authority

asr-003531
04:05:12.483 --> 04:05:14.440
Rep. Marlo C. Bancoro: Now, sir, it is on the part of the Armed Forces. Batay kung doon sa

asr-003532
04:05:18.338 --> 04:05:31.619
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: guidance namin and ini-re-scope ng lahat ng AFP units ang kanilang areas of operation

asr-003533
04:05:32.699 --> 04:05:36.800
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: based on logistics requirements namin.

asr-003534
04:05:37.947 --> 04:05:54.518
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Uh, [unclear].

asr-003535
04:05:56.071 --> 04:06:04.711
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Uh, now, given the parochial concern, anyway...

asr-003537
04:06:04.964 --> 04:06:12.153
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: So, based on the guidance that we gave to them because I don't want to divert

asr-003538
04:06:12.743 --> 04:06:23.172
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: the attention to the major logistical needs of the Armed Forces that we really need to pay attention to

asr-003539
04:06:23.695 --> 04:06:30.293
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: because even the resupply of the base that you will do will be affected if you don't start with

asr-003540
04:06:31.711 --> 04:06:35.440
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: our major logistical bases.

asr-003541
04:06:36.892 --> 04:06:42.359
Rep. Marlo C. Bancoro: Uh, Madam Chair, may I approach them to discuss? Anyway, this is just one minute.

asr-003542
04:06:42.359 --> 04:07:44.527
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Cong., thank you. Thank you. Meeting suspended.

asr-003543
04:19:39.638 --> 04:19:54.286
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Okay, next to interpolate, Vice Chair Anna York Bondoc. Vice Chair Anna York Bondoc.

asr-003543-b
04:20:30.000 --> 04:20:31.100
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Thank you so much.

asr-003544
04:20:32.700 --> 04:20:51.340
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Okay na. Magandang hapon po, Mr. Secretary and the DND family. Thank you so much for the opportunity for us to be able to work closely with you and support your 2027 budget.

asr-003545
04:20:52.060 --> 04:20:55.580
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: First of all, I would like to greet our new AFP Chief of Staff.

asr-003546
04:20:56.580 --> 04:21:04.460
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Nag-meet po kami for the first time and I had the pleasure of meeting him for the first time last year in Bongabon, Nueva Ecija

asr-003547
04:21:04.460 --> 04:21:08.020
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: with the 703rd Agila Brigade.

asr-003548
04:21:08.020 --> 04:21:17.720
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: At nagkita po kami because I wanted to express my support and thanks po to the 7th Infantry Division last year

asr-003549
04:21:17.720 --> 04:21:24.740
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: and the brigade and the battalion [unclear] sa baha.

asr-003550
04:21:24.740 --> 04:21:28.860
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: So, I thought last year was the worst thing that ever happened to me.

asr-003551
04:21:29.420 --> 04:21:36.620
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Ayun pala, this year it was going to be worse. So, I have a few pictures in case you're interested po to see.

asr-003552
04:21:36.780 --> 04:21:46.220
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Up to today po, I come from the 4th District of Pampanga, which is the catch basin po, lahat po ng tubig from Aurora.

asr-003553
04:21:47.400 --> 04:22:03.840
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Ayan po si Kong Angara. Yung tubig niyo bumabagsak sa amin. Yung buong Nueva Ecija po. buong province of Bulacan, and even the Sierra Madre Mountains. So the amount of water pouring in is truly tremendous.

asr-003554
04:22:04.780 --> 04:22:21.880
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: So ayan po ang tumutulong po sa amin. Pakita ninyo iyong baha mismo, iyong plaza po namin iyan. So yan, and that is, later on I will speak to you about MacArthur Highway. So it was actually a good thing.

asr-003564
04:22:21.880 --> 04:22:30.440
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: I had never worked with the Philippine Army previous to last year and I was very grateful sa kanila pong efficiency

asr-003565
04:22:32.900 --> 04:22:38.400
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: and ang bilis po nilang kumilos and most of all their compassion towards us.

asr-003566
04:22:38.680 --> 04:22:44.160
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: So from someone who previously didn't know much about the Army, it was really a revelation to me.

asr-003567
04:22:45.100 --> 04:22:48.900
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: So, ang maganda po from what happened last year,

asr-003568
04:22:49.820 --> 04:22:55.900
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: I am of the philosophy that kung kumikilos ka, pag may baha, huli ka na.

asr-003569
04:22:56.040 --> 04:23:05.280
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: In other words, it is better to prepare for a disaster rather than, even though ang dami hung tumulong, mali pa po yun and that we need to prepare.

asr-003570
04:23:05.580 --> 04:23:07.600
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: So, I would like to again commend,

asr-003571
04:23:07.600 --> 04:23:18.000
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: And nagkaroon po kami ng malawakang Bantay Sapa, or the largest coastal cleanup of Manila Bay. Hindi po makalabas

asr-003572
04:23:18.000 --> 04:23:23.520
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: yung tubig sa amin because of siltation po sa mga sapa. So this last

asr-003573
04:23:23.520 --> 04:23:31.020
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: June, ako po ang nagpondo, lahat po ng tupad ko, pinondohan namin more than 1,500 tupad members.

asr-003574
04:23:32.740 --> 04:23:39.160
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Last [unclear] slide, please. More than 1,500 tupad members po joined us dun sa Bantay Sapa.

asr-003575
04:23:39.380 --> 04:23:41.380
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: This is already the third year.

asr-003576
04:23:41.640 --> 04:23:44.200
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: So we have been doing this for the last three years.

asr-003577
04:23:44.240 --> 04:23:46.100
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Hindi po kami kumikilos dahil may baha.

asr-003578
04:23:46.700 --> 04:23:49.820
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Kumikilos po kami bago po magkabaha.

asr-003586
04:23:50.100 --> 04:23:58.420
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: So you can see this is the Philippine Army, the Philippine Coast Guard, and the Philippine Navy with the DENR and the local government.

asr-003587
04:23:58.640 --> 04:24:05.120
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: So nagkaroon po kami ng Memorandum of Understanding. And I would like to thank Philippine Army,

asr-003588
04:24:05.280 --> 04:24:09.320
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Philippine Navy, ayan po, Coast Guard, at lahat po ng tumulong sa amin.

asr-003589
04:24:09.460 --> 04:24:13.620
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: So year one, we were able to clear 9,000 basura.

asr-003590
04:24:13.660 --> 04:24:17.020
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Year two, 17,000. And year three, 15,000.

asr-003591
04:24:17.400 --> 04:24:21.580
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: So despite all of that, binaha pa rin po kami this year.

asr-003592
04:24:21.780 --> 04:24:26.200
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: So I would personally like to thank, again, I would like to personally mention

asr-003593
04:24:26.200 --> 04:24:32.680
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: [unclear], General Osias, and our battalion commander,

asr-003594
04:24:32.680 --> 04:24:36.320
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: si Lieutenant Colonel [unclear], for their kindness po this year.

asr-003595
04:24:36.320 --> 04:24:40.460
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Hindi lang po sila kind, they are very efficient at mabilis pong kumilos.

asr-003596
04:24:40.680 --> 04:24:53.040
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: So, Secretary, pinupugayan po namin sila sa kanila pong kasipagan at kabaitan sa amin. So, wala po akong masyadong tanong. I would just like to thank them.

asr-003598
04:24:53.180 --> 04:25:02.460
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: I would also like to mention an incident po nang nangyari. One of the ways to prevent flood po is through dredging.

asr-003599
04:25:02.460 --> 04:25:11.560
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: and palabas po yung tubig namin sa Manila Bay. And personally po, nagka-problema na rin po pala ang Philippine Navy sa Manila Bay

asr-003600
04:25:11.560 --> 04:25:17.360
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: because of the siltation. So tinulungan po namin sila and we were very happy to work with them

asr-003601
04:25:18.140 --> 04:25:23.460
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: to dredge po, grabe na po ang siltation, pati po ang Philippine Navy tinamaan na rin po.

asr-003602
04:25:23.620 --> 04:25:29.120
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: And we had to dredge together yung pagdating po ng kanilang destroyer.

asr-003603
04:25:30.740 --> 04:25:41.280
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: So upon conversation po with former Commodore, now present Admiral, tama po ba ako Admiral Nera

asr-003604
04:25:43.180 --> 04:25:55.700
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: nagkausap po kami and nalaman po namin and I told him that if Manila [unclear] silted, and if our destroyers, and we are modernizing the Navy, at mas malalim pa

asr-003605
04:25:55.700 --> 04:25:58.900
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: siguro yung kailangan po nating volume of tubig, tama po ba ako?

asr-003606
04:25:59.200 --> 04:26:05.560
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: So, therefore, dredgers are a very important component po, and very much badly needed by our Navy.

asr-003607
04:26:06.420 --> 04:26:15.500
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: So, Sec, nagka-intindihan po kami that the Philippine Navy needs to purchase dredgers. Kasi po, I told them,

asr-003608
04:26:15.540 --> 04:26:27.080
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: if we are going to purchase large ships, kailangan po talaga ng dredgers. So, I hope you could support the much-needed dredgers po ng Philippine Navy.

asr-003609
04:26:30.480 --> 04:26:39.240
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Of course, Madam Chair, because we really need it also for our own naval bases and ports. There's one in the pipeline

asr-003610
04:26:39.240 --> 04:26:41.220
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: right now, coming in.

asr-003611
04:26:41.440 --> 04:26:57.220
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Opo. Actually, medyo nagkaagawan nga po ng dredger. Kasi we need naman to dredge sa Manila Bay. Kasi babahain kami. But we gladly lent our dredger po to the Philippine Navy.

asr-003612
04:26:57.220 --> 04:27:07.180
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: So tinanong po sa akin [unclear] kataas yung dredger na kailangan. And then they said 1991 pa daw yung pinag-agawan namin. So

asr-003613
04:27:07.180 --> 04:27:09.320
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: it would be really a good idea. May isang suggestion po ako

asr-003614
04:27:09.320 --> 04:27:27.240
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: na madali. Lahat po ng nase-seize na illegal dredgers lagyan ninyo ng exception sa Tariff and Customs code na imbis na isubasta iyan, dalhin na lang sa Coast Guard at saka sa Navy lahat ng [unclear] ng mga dredgers para magamit ho natin.

asr-003615
04:27:28.840 --> 04:27:32.940
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: Kasi kailangan isubasta eh under the Tariff and Customs Code.

asr-003616
04:27:33.160 --> 04:27:39.100
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: So minsan, kapag nakaka-seize ng vessels na malalaki, sinusubasta ito.

asr-003617
04:27:39.880 --> 04:27:43.340
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: And then, nariregurgitate o narirecycle.

asr-003618
04:27:43.760 --> 04:28:16.100
Rep. Anna York P. Bondoc, M.D.: So, kung puwede, [unclear] na lang ho iyan, lalo na pag kailangan ng Navy o ng Coast Guard or ng DENR, for example. Depending on the size, na illegal na mga vessels na imbis na mandatory na isubasta, i-turnover po kung magagamit. Mas [unclear], malaking tulong din po sa atin iyan. Thank you po. And sana po masuportahan niyo po yung purchase of dredgers kasi kailangan po ng Navy.

asr-003621
04:28:17.600 --> 04:28:19.060
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Okay, thank you so much po.

asr-003622
04:28:20.920 --> 04:28:22.940
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Thank you, Vice Chair Anna York Bondoc.

asr-003623
04:28:23.740 --> 04:28:26.720
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Next to interpellate, Congressman Jay Vergara.

asr-003624
04:28:27.780 --> 04:28:32.315
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: Thank you, Chair. Magandang tanghali po sa [unclear].

asr-003626
04:28:32.770 --> 04:28:56.400
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: At susugan ko lang po yung sinabi ni Congresswoman Ana. Regional problem mo yung pinag-uusapan. Dahil minalas tayo ng ating mga bundok ay hinayaan nating kalbuhin na tayo rin ang may kasalanan.

asr-003629
04:28:56.400 --> 04:29:04.951
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: Sakit ho ng konti kung Jay, kalbuhin. Medyo bawasan ng tira, tatamaan po kayo.

asr-003631
04:29:04.951 --> 04:29:16.038
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Medyo malapit na rin doon, eh. Malapit na, eh. Kaya medyo kayo, nangingitim pa pati bigote, tinutubuan. Kanina pa ho ninyo akong niloloko roon sa bigote ko, eh.

asr-003636
04:29:16.055 --> 04:29:22.872
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: Hindi ko po niloloko; nangingitim lang po.

asr-003637
04:29:24.620 --> 04:29:38.020
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: Anyway po, ang pinakamataas po na peak ay si General Pasamonte at si General Osias ay mga kaibigan ko rin po.

asr-003638
04:29:40.140 --> 04:29:55.800
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: Ang pinakamataas na peak doon sa amin sa Nueva Ecija po, ang pangalan po ay Paatas Peak sa Mount Kimalugong. Para po maintindihan po ng lahat.

asr-003643
04:29:55.820 --> 04:29:59.940
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: Sa Mount Kemalugong, ito po ay parte ng Sierra Madre.

asr-003644
04:30:01.100 --> 04:30:05.340
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: Bago dumating ng Caraballo, tapos didiretso sa Cordillera.

asr-003645
04:30:06.340 --> 04:30:13.800
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: So ang dahilan po ng pagbaha ay zero meters above sea level dito sa Metro Manila.

asr-003646
04:30:14.400 --> 04:30:16.880
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: Alin po ba ang zero meter above sea level?

asr-003647
04:30:17.140 --> 04:30:20.380
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: Ang zero meter po ay Manila Bay.

asr-003648
04:30:21.140 --> 04:30:25.780
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: Kaya po yun ang katotohanan kung bakit talaga binabaha tayo.

asr-003649
04:30:26.770 --> 04:30:27.240
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: Ano ho?

asr-003650
04:30:27.840 --> 04:30:40.240
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: Yung bulubundukin na pagka ho may problema ng konti, dire diretsyo yan.

asr-003651
04:30:41.520 --> 04:30:44.120
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: Pagka naligo ka, dire-diretsyo yan.

asr-003653
04:30:45.020 --> 04:30:55.340
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: [unclear] sa Paatas Peak, it's 1,750 meters above sea level.

asr-003654
04:30:55.840 --> 04:31:04.840
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: At ang pinagsusukatan po ng Metro Manila ay Manila Bay, which is zero meter above sea level.

asr-003655
04:31:05.180 --> 04:31:13.180
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: Para ho siyang Luneta na doon nagsisimula yung zero nung kilometrahe.

asr-003656
04:31:13.720 --> 04:31:14.240
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: Ano po?

asr-003657
04:31:14.680 --> 04:31:19.740
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: So, pinag-aralan po namin mabuti yung distrito namin.

asr-003658
04:31:20.160 --> 04:31:34.860
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: Mula sa Bongabon, sa Gabaldon, sa Laur, sa Natividad, sa Palayan, at sa Cabanatuan City po. Tutuloy po ito ng Santa Rosa. Tutuloy po ito sa dalawang river.

asr-003661
04:31:36.140 --> 04:31:43.540
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: Sa gawi po ng 4th District of Nueva Ecija, yung po ay Peñaranda–Rio Chico River.

asr-003662
04:31:44.120 --> 04:31:49.260
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: Pero pupunta rin po siya sa Pampanga River.

asr-003663
04:31:50.160 --> 04:31:53.180
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: Kaya iiyak po talaga yung taga-Pampanga.

asr-003664
04:31:53.360 --> 04:32:12.800
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: Yung pong distrito ng ating chairwoman sa appropriations, kay Chairwoman Mika, yung po ay sa Bongabon maghihiwalay.

asr-003667
04:32:12.800 --> 04:32:31.260
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: Yung sa Talavera River, yung papunta naman po sa amin sa Cabanatuan, sa Cabanatuan bababa. Pero pagka pinag-aralan ninyong mabuti, diretsyo rin po siya doon sa Pampanga River.

asr-003669
04:32:31.260 --> 04:32:43.080
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: Babahain ang sampung bayan ng Tarlac. Babahain ang sampung bayan ng Pampanga.

asr-003671
04:32:43.080 --> 04:32:55.200
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: Pagkatapos, di diretsyong sigurado sa Bulacan at hahanap kasi ng level sa Manila Bay na kung sa naroon ang zero meter above sea level.

asr-003672
04:32:55.540 --> 04:33:20.540
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: So, sinusugan ko lamang po kay Kong Ana yung kanya pong sinasabi para po maintindihan rin po ninyo. Alam ko po yung posisyon ng Department of National Defense hinggil po doon sa ating Fort Magsaysay area.

asr-003674
04:33:20.540 --> 04:33:40.580
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: Pero yung concern po ng Gabaldon, ng Dingalan, nila Kong Rommel Angara po, yung concern po ng Bongabon, Gabaldon, Laur, Santa Rosa, Cabanatuan City...

asr-003675
04:33:40.580 --> 04:34:03.920
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: Hindi po kasama ang Natividad, Peñaranda, at saka General Tinio, ay yung pong 44,341.637 hectares na kasama po sa Fort Magsaysay Reserve.

asr-003676
04:34:05.200 --> 04:34:21.900
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: So, ako po ay siguro ako na po ang huling magsalita. Kung may sususog pa po sa akin, ako po ay sumusuporta lamang po sa inyong pagtulong sa amin parati.

asr-003678
04:34:21.900 --> 04:34:46.700
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: Ang akin lamang po ay hilingin ko lang na makausap po namin, Secretary, kung sino po talaga ang magiging representative ng Department of Defense o ng Army hinggil dito sa usaping ito.

asr-003680
04:34:46.700 --> 04:35:14.200
Rep. Julius Cesar "Jay" V. Vergara: Kasi ang pupunta po sa mga mayor namin sa Palayan, sa Gabaldon, sa General Tinio, sa Laur, sa Peñaranda, sa Santa Rosa, sa Dingalan, at saka sa Cabanatuan ay hindi po nagpupunta yung inyong mismong tao para mapag-usapan po nang maayos itong usapin na ito.

asr-003683
04:35:14.200 --> 04:35:15.104
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Thank you, Kong Jay.

asr-003684
04:35:15.104 --> 04:35:39.440
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Dahil na-realize ko yung concern, really, sa Fort Magsaysay na kailangan ng Armed Forces ngayon, pero ito'y kailangan din sa connectivity ng dalawang lalawigan. At may flood-control implications na kailangan solbahin natin lahat, kasi hindi rin naman puwedeng mabaha yung area o pagdaluyan.

asr-003686
04:35:40.440 --> 04:35:58.360
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Hinggil dito, humingi lang ako ng paumanin sapagkat nagkulang kami ng tao kaya nga po ni-raise natin ang isang opisina dun sa real estate management sa DND level na USEC para makabuild ng ecosystem si dating Assistant Secretary Ramos.

asr-003687
04:35:58.360 --> 04:36:13.880
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Inangat po natin na USEC kasi yung real estate management nagiging malaking... ...issue na kailangan harapin.

asr-003689
04:36:15.120 --> 04:36:23.780
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Ganun po, ganun man din, ang talagang point person dito ay dapat yung installation and management command ng Philippine Army.

asr-003690
04:36:23.780 --> 04:36:28.940
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Kung sino ang nagsusupervise dito.

asr-003691
04:36:29.840 --> 04:36:41.400
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: So, hiling ko muna sa IMCOM within the week, can you establish base with Congressman Vergara? And Congressman Angara.

asr-003693
04:36:42.480 --> 04:36:49.440
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: And can you create the flow mechanism to try to solve the issue?

asr-003694
04:36:49.440 --> 04:36:57.980
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: If the issue is really flood control, I will raise it up to DPWH or whatever agency.

asr-003695
04:36:58.380 --> 04:37:13.300
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: But at least there must be a flow already because until we are able to support and staff under Secretary Ramos' team... ...to support him, kulang na kulang kami talaga.

asr-003697
04:37:14.300 --> 04:37:15.640
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Nandiyan ba si Eman? Wala.

asr-003703
04:37:15.640 --> 04:37:41.900
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Ah, naka-leave. Naka-leave. Naka-leave. But siya po ay nagpapahinga lang dahil talagang kawawa rin yung tao. We have about live real estate issues, mga halos tatlong daan. Tapos 40,000 ba yung dine-defend natin, na-ejectment cases, so forth and so on.

asr-003705
04:37:41.900 --> 04:37:51.360
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: So, pati OSG po nagre-reklamo na doon sa amin. Ngunit, ito na po ang aking [unclear].

asr-003707
04:37:51.500 --> 04:38:06.760
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Within the week, can you ask your IMCOM to meet with Congressman Vergara and Congressman Angara? And submit to me monthly progress reports on the issues and what happens. Maraming salamat po.

asr-003710
04:38:07.212 --> 04:38:09.750
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Madam Chair, can I interject with the Congressman?

asr-003711
04:38:09.760 --> 04:38:09.963
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Yes.

asr-003712
04:38:09.963 --> 04:38:14.540
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Thank you. Maraming salamat po. First and foremost, maraming maraming salamat po, Secretary Gibo Teodoro.

asr-003714
04:38:15.740 --> 04:38:19.980
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Before I begin, ako po ay nagpapasalamat sa ating Armed Forces of the Philippines.

asr-003715
04:38:20.120 --> 04:38:31.600
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: In fact, kami po sa lalawigan ng Aurora, sa Lone District of Aurora, kami ata yung unang nag-build ng buong buo yung ating camp ng ating Armed Forces of the Philippines.

asr-003716
04:38:32.340 --> 04:38:37.760
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Gusto ko lang pong dagdagan yung sinabi ni Congressman Jay Vergara na binanggit po niya dun sa ating military reservation.

asr-003717
04:38:38.900 --> 04:38:44.620
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Yes. We've known for a fact that ito po ay pagmamay-ari ng ating base militar.

asr-003719
04:38:45.000 --> 04:38:51.180
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: But earlier, hindi ko po alam na magsasalita si Congressman Jay because I was supposed to go to the other committee hearing.

asr-003720
04:38:51.320 --> 04:38:58.280
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: But I approached USEC Gavin, which was given to me by our Chair Bella.

asr-003721
04:38:58.280 --> 04:39:12.660
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Ang aking hiling lang po is because for the past 47 years, ang aming probinsya po, ang lalawigan ng Aurora, before ay maraming insurgents. But now, halos nawala na po ito.

asr-003724
04:39:12.760 --> 04:39:23.940
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: My fear, Mr. Secretary, is that because of the ongoing military reservation on the ground level, yung kaninang sinasabi ni Congressman Jay Vergara na nagko-coordinate directly to the mayors.

asr-003726
04:39:24.560 --> 04:39:27.440
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Siguro po, a bit of thought, Mr. Secretary.

asr-003727
04:39:27.440 --> 04:39:31.520
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Sorry. Siguro kami naman po ay willing makipagtulungan sa ating Armed Forces of the Philippines.

asr-003728
04:39:31.680 --> 04:39:37.420
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: In fact, ang sabi ko po kay Yusek Gavin kanina, I think there's a proper way on how to do it.

asr-003729
04:39:37.960 --> 04:39:47.460
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: In fact, like for example sa Aurora po, if I'm not mistaken, there's around 6,000-plus hectares sa military reservation sa tatlo o apat na barangay.

asr-003731
04:39:47.720 --> 04:39:51.480
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: And this comprises around 3,000 families na madi-displace.

asr-003732
04:39:51.860 --> 04:39:56.020
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Pero pag sabi ko, ako, I've always been optimistic on how government works.

asr-003733
04:39:56.020 --> 04:40:05.820
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Sabi ko, pag nagtulungan naman ang LGU, myself, the Department of Defense, even the Office of the President, I think there is a right way or procedure on how to do things.

asr-003735
04:40:06.020 --> 04:40:10.600
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Kasi po, I'll be honest with you, Mr. Secretary, may mga bahay na pong nandoon po talaga.

asr-003737
04:40:10.900 --> 04:40:18.800
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: So, on our part, as the government, it will be difficult na paalisin sila ng ura-urada.

asr-003738
04:40:18.940 --> 04:40:23.240
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: And hindi naman po tama rin iyon. You've also been a district representative, Mr. Secretary.

asr-003740
04:40:23.240 --> 04:40:26.680
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: So, tayo yung takbuhan ng ating mga kababayan, even the mayor.

asr-003741
04:40:26.800 --> 04:40:47.320
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: So ako po, maraming salamat na sinabi po ninyo na magtatalaga agad kayo ng isang USEC na kakausap sa aming tatlong congressman sa military reservation in Nueva Ecija and Aurora, namely Congressman Jay Vergara, Congressman Emeng Pascual, and for me, the Lone District of the Province of Aurora.

asr-003746
04:40:47.320 --> 04:41:04.805
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Mas maganda po sana na upuan po ito natin. And I think pag inupuan po ng mga leaders po iyan, together with your USEC, undersecretaries, and the people concerned, ay ito po ay mapag-uusapan nang maayos at puwede pa tayong magtulungan moving forward, Mr. Secretary. Iyon lamang po, Mr. Secretary. Maraming salamat.

asr-003751
04:41:04.805 --> 04:41:17.680
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Ito po sa Aurora na pinagtutuunan namin ng pansin. Number one is the boundary between Quezon and Aurora and Rizal, na ang Army ay manipis doon sa area na iyon, pati po Infanta.

asr-003754
04:41:18.608 --> 04:41:25.240
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Secondly is the foreshore area na importante po sa amin, lalo na sa Dingalan.

asr-003755
04:41:26.472 --> 04:41:38.120
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: So kailangan din siguro, on the naval side, Admiral Ezpeleta, tutukan mo ng tao rin kasama ng IMCOM.

asr-003756
04:41:38.120 --> 04:41:40.951
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Okay. Thank you.

asr-003757
04:41:42.470 --> 04:41:43.938
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Thank you, Mr. Secretary. Thank you.

asr-003758
04:41:46.064 --> 04:41:51.498
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Thank you, Vice Chair Rommel Angara and Congressman Jay Vergara.

asr-003759
04:41:52.409 --> 04:41:59.058
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Last to interpellate for the first round, from the majority, Representative Jeffrey Ferrer.

asr-003760
04:42:02.160 --> 04:42:05.920
Rep. Jeffrey P. Ferrer: Thank you very much, Madam Chair.

asr-003761
04:42:05.920 --> 04:42:10.480
Rep. Jeffrey P. Ferrer: Alam ko, exhausted na si Secretary. So kaninang umaga pa to.

asr-003762
04:42:10.480 --> 04:42:14.638
Rep. Jeffrey P. Ferrer: Pero sandali lang to the AFP family. Good afternoon.

asr-003763
04:42:14.638 --> 04:42:20.240
Rep. Jeffrey P. Ferrer: E tanong ko lang, how is peace and order in Negros Island, Secretary?

asr-003764
04:42:20.240 --> 04:42:26.480
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Well, for now, we are seeing some stability in Negros Island.

asr-003765
04:42:26.480 --> 04:42:38.400
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: And we are thankful to the local government for the support of the whole province of Negros Occidental.

asr-003766
04:42:38.400 --> 04:42:46.400
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: For the support for national security.

asr-003767
04:42:46.400 --> 04:42:54.718
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: That being said, on the oriental side, the situation remains stable also.

asr-003768
04:42:54.718 --> 04:43:07.680
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: So we are also likewise thankful for the all-out support of the local government.

asr-003769
04:43:07.680 --> 04:43:13.280
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: And the convergence between the local government.

asr-003770
04:43:13.280 --> 04:43:16.878
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: And the armed forces of the Philippines.

asr-003771
04:43:16.878 --> 04:43:23.840
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Particularly, when we view the situation that Negros, with the continuous degassing of Mount Canlaon,

asr-003772
04:43:23.840 --> 04:43:28.080
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: needs a different kind of attention right now.

asr-003773
04:43:28.080 --> 04:43:32.400
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Where we face severe relocation issues that we need to do.

asr-003774
04:43:32.400 --> 04:43:36.320
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: And we are still rebuilding lives.

asr-003775
04:43:36.320 --> 04:43:42.000
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: So we cannot afford any peace and order disruptions in the area at this time.

asr-003776
04:43:42.000 --> 04:43:43.040
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Thank you very much.

asr-003777
04:43:43.040 --> 04:43:44.080
Rep. Jeffrey P. Ferrer: Thank you very much, Mr. Secretary.

asr-003778
04:43:44.080 --> 04:43:48.080
Rep. Jeffrey P. Ferrer: And then going to OCD.

asr-003779
04:43:48.080 --> 04:43:53.680
Rep. Jeffrey P. Ferrer: Alam mo naman po, in the past months, tinamaan tayo ng Bagyong Tino doon.

asr-003780
04:43:53.680 --> 04:43:59.280
Rep. Jeffrey P. Ferrer: And then na-damage yung malaking damage sa 4th District and 5th District.

asr-003781
04:43:59.280 --> 04:44:13.120
Rep. Jeffrey P. Ferrer: Kamusta yung, is there an ongoing project or rehabilitation sa mga areas na na-damage ng Bagyong Tino?

asr-003782
04:44:13.120 --> 04:44:16.858
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Ngayon, yung rehabilitation kong is, sa amin,

asr-003783
04:44:16.858 --> 04:44:18.617
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: is response sa amin.

asr-003784
04:44:18.617 --> 04:44:23.440
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Sa rehabilitation, nagkaroon sila ng Negros ay yung Canlaon Rehabilitation Plan.

asr-003785
04:44:23.440 --> 04:44:27.290
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: But it lacks sufficient detail for me.

asr-003786
04:44:27.290 --> 04:44:29.920
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Kaya sinuli ko muna sa kanila.

asr-003787
04:44:29.920 --> 04:44:36.638
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: And the most important thing on the Canlaon issue is the acquisition of land for relocation.

asr-003788
04:44:36.638 --> 04:44:39.190
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: In areas which are not affected.

asr-003789
04:44:39.200 --> 04:44:44.390
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: And I think they identified some areas on the...

asr-003790
04:44:44.400 --> 04:44:48.470
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: 5th or 6th District.

asr-003791
04:44:48.480 --> 04:44:51.590
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: or 6th District, I believe.

asr-003792
04:44:51.600 --> 04:44:53.500
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Doon sa 4th,

asr-003793
04:44:53.500 --> 04:44:55.500
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: doon sa rehabilitation,

asr-003794
04:44:55.500 --> 04:44:57.830
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: ito ay hindi na nanggagaling sa amin,

asr-003795
04:44:57.840 --> 04:45:01.110
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: nanggagaling sa mother agencies,

asr-003796
04:45:01.120 --> 04:45:02.868
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: batay sa kautosan ng DBM.

asr-003797
04:45:03.600 --> 04:45:04.718
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Nonetheless,

asr-003798
04:45:05.520 --> 04:45:08.948
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: OCD-NIR

asr-003799
04:45:08.958 --> 04:45:13.430
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: is tasked to continuously coordinate

asr-003800
04:45:13.440 --> 04:45:16.868
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: with OCD Central

asr-003801
04:45:16.878 --> 04:45:20.390
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: to prod the other agencies for action.

asr-003802
04:45:20.400 --> 04:45:24.070
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: For example, with Congresswoman Ana Bondoc,

asr-003803
04:45:24.080 --> 04:45:27.270
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: I raised the attention of the flooding

asr-003804
04:45:27.280 --> 04:45:31.270
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: to Secretary Dizon by official communication

asr-003805
04:45:31.280 --> 04:45:34.958
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: so that it can be addressed systematically.

asr-003806
04:45:36.320 --> 04:45:38.400
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Your Honor.

asr-003807
04:45:38.400 --> 04:45:39.200
Rep. Jeffrey P. Ferrer: Thank you, Sec.

asr-003808
04:45:39.200 --> 04:45:42.339
Rep. Jeffrey P. Ferrer: Because napakagaling mo

asr-003809
04:45:42.339 --> 04:45:43.103
Rep. Jeffrey P. Ferrer: at saka advantageous

asr-003810
04:45:43.103 --> 04:45:43.840
Rep. Jeffrey P. Ferrer: ka talaga,

asr-003811
04:45:43.840 --> 04:45:44.949
Rep. Jeffrey P. Ferrer: yung next question ko

asr-003812
04:45:44.949 --> 04:45:46.798
Rep. Jeffrey P. Ferrer: yung sa OPLAN-Kanlaon natin.

asr-003813
04:45:46.798 --> 04:45:49.399
Rep. Jeffrey P. Ferrer: That is why sinabi mo na

asr-003814
04:45:49.399 --> 04:45:51.440
Rep. Jeffrey P. Ferrer: yung mga areas,

asr-003815
04:45:51.440 --> 04:45:54.339
Rep. Jeffrey P. Ferrer: kasi yung even in La Carlota City,

asr-003816
04:45:54.339 --> 04:45:55.799
Rep. Jeffrey P. Ferrer: part ng kung minsan

asr-003817
04:45:55.799 --> 04:45:57.459
Rep. Jeffrey P. Ferrer: kung pumutok yung Kanlaon,

asr-003818
04:45:57.459 --> 04:45:59.158
Rep. Jeffrey P. Ferrer: doon mismo pumupunta,

asr-003819
04:45:59.158 --> 04:46:00.638
Rep. Jeffrey P. Ferrer: especially La Castellana

asr-003820
04:46:00.638 --> 04:46:01.680
Rep. Jeffrey P. Ferrer: in the 5th District.

asr-003821
04:46:01.680 --> 04:46:02.958
Rep. Jeffrey P. Ferrer: But anyway,

asr-003822
04:46:02.958 --> 04:46:04.676
Rep. Jeffrey P. Ferrer: with regards to that,

asr-003823
04:46:04.676 --> 04:46:07.254
Rep. Jeffrey P. Ferrer: parang nag-re-remind lang ako

asr-003824
04:46:07.254 --> 04:46:10.878
Rep. Jeffrey P. Ferrer: na hindi kami din makalimutan doon

asr-003825
04:46:10.878 --> 04:46:14.480
Rep. Jeffrey P. Ferrer: because some of our requests,

asr-003826
04:46:14.480 --> 04:46:16.940
Rep. Jeffrey P. Ferrer: as already mga bridges natin,

asr-003827
04:46:16.940 --> 04:46:18.400
Rep. Jeffrey P. Ferrer: nakita ko na sa NEP ng DPWH,

asr-003828
04:46:18.400 --> 04:46:23.040
Rep. Jeffrey P. Ferrer: but it was already 2 years na proposal.

asr-003829
04:46:23.040 --> 04:46:24.080
Rep. Jeffrey P. Ferrer: And then ngayon pa lang,

asr-003830
04:46:24.080 --> 04:46:24.456
Rep. Jeffrey P. Ferrer: 2027,

asr-003831
04:46:24.456 --> 04:46:25.725
Rep. Jeffrey P. Ferrer: pero kawawa yung iba

asr-003832
04:46:25.725 --> 04:46:31.269
Rep. Jeffrey P. Ferrer: kasi nasira yung mga bridges doon,

asr-003833
04:46:31.269 --> 04:46:32.984
Rep. Jeffrey P. Ferrer: kawawa yung isang community

asr-003834
04:46:32.984 --> 04:46:37.096
Rep. Jeffrey P. Ferrer: na parang mga kabataan doon,

asr-003835
04:46:37.096 --> 04:46:39.680
Rep. Jeffrey P. Ferrer: doon pa nag-aaral sa kabilang bayan.

asr-003836
04:46:39.680 --> 04:46:41.626
Rep. Jeffrey P. Ferrer: So that is the only access

asr-003837
04:46:41.626 --> 04:46:42.931
Rep. Jeffrey P. Ferrer: na hindi,

asr-003838
04:46:42.931 --> 04:46:45.590
Rep. Jeffrey P. Ferrer: na tatawid sila.

asr-003839
04:46:45.590 --> 04:46:48.718
Rep. Jeffrey P. Ferrer: So kung nasira na yung bridge doon,

asr-003840
04:46:48.718 --> 04:46:49.520
Rep. Jeffrey P. Ferrer: they have no choice

asr-003841
04:46:49.520 --> 04:46:52.798
Rep. Jeffrey P. Ferrer: is to cross that river.

asr-003842
04:46:52.798 --> 04:46:54.638
Rep. Jeffrey P. Ferrer: So anyway,

asr-003843
04:46:54.638 --> 04:46:57.901
Rep. Jeffrey P. Ferrer: I hope na ikaw familiar ka rin doon

asr-003844
04:46:57.901 --> 04:47:01.600
Rep. Jeffrey P. Ferrer: at saka pamilya ka na ng Negros.

asr-003845
04:47:01.600 --> 04:47:02.400
Rep. Jeffrey P. Ferrer: So just a reminder.

asr-003846
04:47:02.400 --> 04:47:04.000
Rep. Jeffrey P. Ferrer: Thank you very much, Madam Speaker.

asr-003847
04:47:04.000 --> 04:47:04.798
Rep. Jeffrey P. Ferrer: Thank you, Secretary.

asr-003848
04:47:04.798 --> 04:47:06.958
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: That is the level of detail, Your Honor,

asr-003849
04:47:06.958 --> 04:47:08.480
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: that I would have wanted to see

asr-003850
04:47:08.480 --> 04:47:10.240
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: in the rehabilitation plan.

asr-003851
04:47:10.240 --> 04:47:13.040
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: But unfortunately, I did not see it.

asr-003852
04:47:13.040 --> 04:47:15.360
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: So I returned it.

asr-003853
04:47:15.360 --> 04:47:17.200
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Well, anyway, your representative

asr-003854
04:47:17.200 --> 04:47:21.120
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: and NIR will keep on communicating

asr-003855
04:47:21.120 --> 04:47:21.879
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: with the LGUs.

asr-003856
04:47:21.879 --> 04:47:22.395
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Yes, Your Honor.

asr-003857
04:47:22.395 --> 04:47:27.040
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Tayo naman ang representante dito

asr-003858
04:47:27.040 --> 04:47:30.718
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: is to air all those problems

asr-003859
04:47:30.718 --> 04:47:33.280
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: in national agencies.

asr-003860
04:47:33.280 --> 04:47:34.400
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Thank you very much, Secretary.

asr-003861
04:47:34.400 --> 04:47:38.320
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Thank you, Your Honor.

asr-003862
04:47:38.320 --> 04:47:40.560
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Thank you, Count Jeffrey Ferrer.

asr-003863
04:47:40.560 --> 04:47:42.000
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Next to interpolate

asr-003864
04:47:42.000 --> 04:47:43.660
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: is Congressman Tonypet Albano.

asr-003867
04:47:44.080 --> 04:47:47.700
Rep. Antonio "Tonypet" T. Albano: Thank you, Chair. Actually, it's not an interpolation

asr-003868
04:47:47.740 --> 04:47:48.600
Rep. Antonio "Tonypet" T. Albano: but more of a

asr-003869
04:47:50.520 --> 04:47:51.520
Rep. Antonio "Tonypet" T. Albano: giving my

asr-003870
04:47:52.180 --> 04:47:53.340
Rep. Antonio "Tonypet" T. Albano: trust and confidence

asr-003871
04:47:53.340 --> 04:47:54.220
Rep. Antonio "Tonypet" T. Albano: to the Secretary

asr-003872
04:47:54.220 --> 04:47:55.780
Rep. Antonio "Tonypet" T. Albano: for doing a good job,

asr-003873
04:47:55.940 --> 04:47:57.160
Rep. Antonio "Tonypet" T. Albano: especially the AFP.

asr-003874
04:47:58.880 --> 04:48:00.500
Rep. Antonio "Tonypet" T. Albano: And good afternoon,

asr-003875
04:48:00.660 --> 04:48:01.880
Rep. Antonio "Tonypet" T. Albano: Sir Gilbert

asr-003876
04:48:02.920 --> 04:48:04.760
Rep. Antonio "Tonypet" T. Albano: and your Chief of Staff

asr-003877
04:48:05.000 --> 04:48:05.680
Rep. Antonio "Tonypet" T. Albano: whom we've

asr-003878
04:48:05.680 --> 04:48:08.620
Rep. Antonio "Tonypet" T. Albano: confirmed in the CA recently.

asr-003879
04:48:09.260 --> 04:48:10.460
Rep. Antonio "Tonypet" T. Albano: And congratulations

asr-003880
04:48:10.460 --> 04:48:11.700
Rep. Antonio "Tonypet" T. Albano: to my cousin,

asr-003881
04:48:11.960 --> 04:48:28.300
Rep. Antonio "Tonypet" T. Albano: Lieutenant General Donald Gumiran for... [unclear]. But more than anything, Secretary, I talked to your Chief of Staff, si Toto, General Toto, who was asking

asr-003885
04:48:28.300 --> 04:49:00.000
Rep. Antonio "Tonypet" T. Albano: How we can strengthen your engineering brigade, because if you remember history, Europe and even Asia was built by the Marshall Plan. And if you have a strong engineering brigade that you have there, and we can add budgets, then you will be more receptive not only to help in disaster mitigation, especially in cases where flooding is there, but more so during...

asr-003904
04:49:00.000 --> 04:49:02.480
Rep. Antonio "Tonypet" T. Albano: the non-delicate seasons

asr-003905
04:49:02.480 --> 04:49:03.840
Rep. Antonio "Tonypet" T. Albano: where there's no typhoon,

asr-003906
04:49:03.880 --> 04:49:04.860
Rep. Antonio "Tonypet" T. Albano: we can use the engineers

asr-003907
04:49:04.860 --> 04:49:07.020
Rep. Antonio "Tonypet" T. Albano: to actually rehabilitate

asr-003908
04:49:07.020 --> 04:49:08.100
Rep. Antonio "Tonypet" T. Albano: a lot of areas

asr-003909
04:49:08.100 --> 04:49:08.820
Rep. Antonio "Tonypet" T. Albano: in the Philippines,

asr-003910
04:49:08.940 --> 04:49:09.840
Rep. Antonio "Tonypet" T. Albano: especially a particular

asr-003911
04:49:10.520 --> 04:49:11.340
Rep. Antonio "Tonypet" T. Albano: airline like what you did

asr-003912
04:49:11.340 --> 04:49:14.480
Rep. Antonio "Tonypet" T. Albano: in Mindalao.

asr-003913
04:49:14.620 --> 04:49:22.960
Rep. Antonio "Tonypet" T. Albano: So, I'd just like to ask, Secretary, if you'd be able to help us create some type of Marshall Plan for your engineering brigade.

asr-003914
04:49:23.180 --> 04:49:24.620
Rep. Antonio "Tonypet" T. Albano: Is that feasible or not?

asr-003915
04:49:24.620 --> 04:49:30.180
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Actually, our engineering brigades are converting into combat engineering brigades,

asr-003916
04:49:30.260 --> 04:49:46.240
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: which are there to allow our equipment to work safely and sustainably.

asr-003917
04:49:46.980 --> 04:49:51.780
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: For example, the emergency bridging that will support our heavy equipment.

asr-003918
04:49:52.640 --> 04:50:00.200
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Secondly, it will be the demining or equipment.

asr-003919
04:50:00.200 --> 04:50:01.460
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Which are engineers.

asr-003920
04:50:02.240 --> 04:50:12.560
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Secondly, if we have them, they should be devoted to base development and not contracted out anymore for civil engineering services.

asr-003921
04:50:12.560 --> 04:50:27.980
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: So, actually, what has happened is we were devoting civil engineering equipment to non-AFP matters.

asr-003922
04:50:27.980 --> 04:50:30.200
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: And our base...

asr-003923
04:50:30.200 --> 04:50:31.040
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Base development suffered.

asr-003924
04:50:31.040 --> 04:50:34.760
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: So, one thing led to another.

asr-003925
04:50:35.900 --> 04:50:52.520
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: Secondly, also, I understand the need for civil engineering, which is why the Army's game plan right now is to increase its footprint in areas which may be unoccupied.

asr-003926
04:50:52.520 --> 04:50:55.320
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: And the first thing you need to do is access.

asr-003927
04:50:55.320 --> 04:50:58.040
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: And the access to the base...

asr-003929
04:50:58.040 --> 04:51:08.600
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: whether it be a division headquarters or a brigade headquarters, will be an all-weather, heavy-duty road access,

asr-003930
04:51:08.600 --> 04:51:11.740
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: which will benefit the economy.

asr-003931
04:51:12.570 --> 04:51:15.000
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: And it will be a connectivity node.

asr-003932
04:51:16.090 --> 04:51:22.440
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: And it will allow resupply, and it will allow presence and deterrence at the same time,

asr-003933
04:51:22.440 --> 04:51:27.820
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: whether it be for deforestation, illegal mining, or what have you.

asr-003934
04:51:27.820 --> 04:51:29.080
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: So, uh...

asr-003935
04:51:29.080 --> 04:51:36.660
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: We have that as a strategic plan because we need to increase the Army's footprint,

asr-003936
04:51:36.660 --> 04:51:45.220
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: and we need strategic basing that will be resupplied by the nodes created on the baselines.

asr-003937
04:51:45.220 --> 04:51:54.540
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: It's part of the integrated defense concept, which will, in turn, benefit the economy because of the all-weather access.

asr-003938
04:51:55.080 --> 04:51:56.340
Rep. Antonio "Tonypet" T. Albano: Thank you. Thank you, Secretary.

asr-003939
04:51:57.020 --> 04:51:58.860
Rep. Antonio "Tonypet" T. Albano: But in terms of disaster,

asr-003940
04:51:59.120 --> 04:52:03.220
Rep. Antonio "Tonypet" T. Albano: I'm sure you're always there because you're head of the NDRMC, if I remember.

asr-003941
04:52:03.780 --> 04:52:09.500
Rep. Antonio "Tonypet" T. Albano: So, like, yung mga basura na nangyayari dito, it's a man-made thing in Metro Manila,

asr-003942
04:52:09.580 --> 04:52:14.520
Rep. Antonio "Tonypet" T. Albano: and sometimes the government is being blamed for not implementing flood controls.

asr-003943
04:52:14.720 --> 04:52:25.340
Rep. Antonio "Tonypet" T. Albano: I'm sure with your help, Secretary, we will hopefully give enough budgets for your engineering brigade to help in that natural disaster, at least.

asr-003944
04:52:25.340 --> 04:52:29.100
Rep. Antonio "Tonypet" T. Albano: Because we are the number one prone disaster country in the whole world.

asr-003945
04:52:29.100 --> 04:52:32.640
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: And, yes, yes, Your Honor, we totally agree.

asr-003946
04:52:32.640 --> 04:52:42.380
Rep. Antonio "Tonypet" T. Albano: And lastly, Madam Chair, we talked also in the Commission on Appointments about the drone program,

asr-003947
04:52:42.380 --> 04:52:50.920
Rep. Antonio "Tonypet" T. Albano: which, of course, it is highly sensitive, and the Chief of Staff has not really given us...

asr-003948
04:52:52.040 --> 04:52:56.200
Rep. Antonio "Tonypet" T. Albano: Well, you're supposed to report to us the progress of the drones.

asr-003949
04:52:56.200 --> 04:52:58.140
Rep. Antonio "Tonypet" T. Albano: Because, as you can understand,

asr-003950
04:52:58.980 --> 04:53:04.360
Rep. Antonio "Tonypet" T. Albano: a small country like Ukraine now can actually fight a superpower like Russia and beat them.

asr-003951
04:53:05.160 --> 04:53:10.440
Rep. Antonio "Tonypet" T. Albano: And if you remember, Secretary, we once talked about this two years ago,

asr-003952
04:53:10.440 --> 04:53:14.500
Rep. Antonio "Tonypet" T. Albano: and I told you that drone technology is the best way we won't lose anything.

asr-003953
04:53:14.820 --> 04:53:18.840
Rep. Antonio "Tonypet" T. Albano: And during armed conflicts, you can send it into critical areas.

asr-003954
04:53:19.080 --> 04:53:22.860
Rep. Antonio "Tonypet" T. Albano: So, I'd like lang the status of this, and I'm in full support.

asr-003955
04:53:23.160 --> 04:53:25.760
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: We're building the framework and the backbone for it.

asr-003956
04:53:26.680 --> 04:53:28.620
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: That's all I can disclose now.

asr-003957
04:53:29.300 --> 04:53:32.660
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: And, you know, as I said, the drones themselves are easy to do.

asr-003958
04:53:33.140 --> 04:53:38.880
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: It's what you put in them, depending on the purpose that we are.

asr-003959
04:53:40.180 --> 04:53:45.520
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: And these are not autonomous devices [unclear], right?

asr-003960
04:53:46.320 --> 04:53:51.520
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: So, we are developing the control systems for it alongside the capabilities.

asr-003961
04:53:52.340 --> 04:53:58.120
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: We do have capabilities [unclear].

asr-003962
04:53:59.420 --> 04:54:09.480
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: And that is well within the engagement framework of the Armed Forces of the Philippines.

asr-003963
04:54:10.540 --> 04:54:12.180
DND Secretary Gilberto C. Teodoro Jr.: That's all I can disclose.

asr-003964
04:54:12.180 --> 04:54:14.120
Rep. Antonio "Tonypet" T. Albano: Thank you, thank you, Mr. Secretary.

asr-003965
04:54:14.120 --> 04:54:20.640
Rep. Antonio "Tonypet" T. Albano: With that, Madam Chairman, this representation is in full support of the Filipino Army and, of course, the DND.

asr-003966
04:54:21.400 --> 04:54:24.720
Rep. Antonio "Tonypet" T. Albano: Kayo po ang heroes ng Pilipino.

asr-003967
04:54:24.720 --> 04:54:30.300
Rep. Antonio "Tonypet" T. Albano: Nakakatulog po kami ng mahingbing dahil sa servisyo na inaalay niyo yung sarili niyong buhay.

asr-003968
04:54:30.300 --> 04:54:35.660
Rep. Antonio "Tonypet" T. Albano: Para sa kapakanan ng ating bansa at mga mamayang Pilipino.

asr-003969
04:54:35.660 --> 04:54:39.380
Rep. Antonio "Tonypet" T. Albano: Kaya saludo po kami at full support po ang House of Representatives.

asr-003970
04:54:40.060 --> 04:54:45.760
Rep. Antonio "Tonypet" T. Albano: Lalo na tinapunta po ako ni Speaker Boji dito para sabihin po sa inyo,

asr-003971
04:54:45.800 --> 04:54:50.180
Rep. Antonio "Tonypet" T. Albano: full support po ang opisina ni Speaker at ang mga congressman dito po.

asr-003972
04:54:50.220 --> 04:54:50.820
Rep. Antonio "Tonypet" T. Albano: Maraming salamat.

asr-003973
